{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories","id":118767,"title":"Your noddist fan theories","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-24T16:56:39-07:00","id":118767,"title":"Your noddist fan theories","content":"I thought we could share some of our own noddist speculations, and ideas that are not explicitly supported by the books. Here are some of mine. May contradict each other:<br /> <br /> The third Baali was Rayzeel. And that was why Saulot commanded his childer &quot;Do not embrace love&quot;<br /> <br /> Ahab going over to the Baali was what he was embraced for by Saulot, to cover for him and Rayzeel in the creation of the Baali. Both those Baali creation stories are true.<br /> <br /> Shaitan from Chaos Factor was Rayzeel. They were both singers at the start. Rayzeel stole Saulots heart singing in the dark before he knew what the pits she was singing to was for.<br /> <br /> Brujah was the first Antediluvian to fake his death. He and Troile together ambushed Ventrue, and Troile diablerized Ventrue. This happened sometime between 1256 and 1250 BC. (Youngest known 4th gen Ventrue/Oldest known 4th gen brujah). Not originally my idea.<br /> <br /> Troile was originally a Torador, and have in fact been confused with Arikel in several genalogies.<br /> <br /> The original Ashur was Saulot. Cappadocious was his first childe, and the bloodline he spawned before he went east. Cappadocious studies lead him to the first diablerie, and the decay his line suffers is the punishment.<br /> <br /> Set was sired a Gangrel of the 4th generation. He diablerized his way to third. The Tlactique are descended from his oldest get, before his diablerie.<br /> <br /> Typhon was Brujah. Osiris description of his emotional deadening matches the Trujah clan flaws and the powers match Potence, Presence and Temporis.<br /> <br /> Set was infuencing a family of Italian necromancers for centuries in the guise of Dis Pater. When he was corporally disadvantaged around year 1, he took up the guise permanently. The Giovannia made strides in Necromancy that would so impress the Cappadocians because they had heavy help from the lands of the dead.<br /> <br /> Osiris physically destroyed Set around the brith of Christ. He had motive, means, opportunity and was speciffically without alibi.<br /> <br /> While Augustus Giovanni believes the True Vessel contains the remaining blood of Cappadocious and the people who participared in the ritual generally believe it to contain the mortal blood of Augustus, only the traitor knew that it contains the remnant of the blood used to embrace Augustus -that of the Lasombra Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As theories, I believe there are few things contradicting them, and lets us face it, established facts in Kindred history have plenty of stuff contradicting them. There are also litte supporting them, but that is what specualtion is for<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What are some of yours?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T17:29:08-07:00","id":118794,"title":"","content":"Not bad. Here are some of my theories.<br /> <br /> A. Malkav was murdered by his childer. There was no unknown assassin. None of then understood the true power of Malkav. E<br /> <br /> B. Verdatha, Antediluvian of the Ventrue is Saulot. Both have a form of Prey Exclusion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T17:32:58-07:00","id":118797,"title":"","content":"The majority of Fragments from the Book of Nod were created whole sale between late antiquity and the medieval period thus why they show significant divergence from works that would match the &quot;proper&quot; time period if they were accurate. This does not mean that they may not be based on older works that were &quot;fixed&quot; by scribes to better match their views of faith/history and the particular lies that elders have latched onto for various personal and political reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then I use this as a basis to start dropping in all sorts of tablets that go completely off the rails because why shouldn't kindred lie constantly about their history?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T18:13:43-07:00","id":118820,"title":"","content":"I'm personally a fan of the &quot;three by ten&quot; translation of the Book of Nod, suggesting somewhere in the neighborhood of thirty Antediluvians as opposed to thirteen. My own personal take on where they went is that the Thirteen are the ones who got off easy by begging mercy from Caine, and the remaining Unrepentant were punished far more unspeakably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T02:18:06-07:00","id":119005,"title":"","content":"I usually count all named Antediluvians from official sources as &quot;real&quot; in the sense that they exist or have existed, because I feel that the world is more interesting with a higher number of strange creatures. I have created a fair bit of history for some of the Antediluvians without Clans of their own, and have even let my players meet some of these obscure ancients at times. In my version of the World of Darkness, Ashur and Saulot are definitely distinct characters, and both Arikel and Ishtar exist as separate Antediluvians. Some of the weird Disciplines &quot;invented&quot; by strange Bloodlines are actually far older than the Bloodlines themselves, having been the signature Disciplines of Antediluvians who did not survive long enough to form Clans. The Disciplines were then either rediscovered by Bloodline founders or kept in play by other ancient Cainites who then created these new Bloodlines for different reasons. Even Daimoinon is such a Discipline in my setting - the Baali were given the Discipline by Saulot when he created them, but it was originally the signature Discipline of one of Saulot's fellow Antediluvians. I have made up a lot of stuff about Malakai in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T04:53:22-07:00","id":119038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories#post118767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought we could share some of our own noddist speculations, and ideas that are not explicitly supported by the books. Here are some of mine. May contradict each other:<br /> <br /> The third Baali was Rayzeel. And that was why Saulot commanded his childer &quot;Do not embrace love&quot; <b>You stole that idea from me, lol. Maybe.</b><br /> <br /> Ahab going over to the Baali was what he was embraced for by Saulot, to cover for him and Rayzeel in the creation of the Baali. Both those Baali creation stories are true. <b>Ahab showed up in onyl one book. I ignore him.</b><br /> <br /> Shaitan from Chaos Factor was Rayzeel. They were both singers at the start. Rayzeel stole Saulots heart singing in the dark before he knew what the pits she was singing to was for. <b>Possible.</b><br /> <br /> Brujah was the first Antediluvian to fake his death. He and Troile together ambushed Ventrue, and Troile diablerized Ventrue. This happened sometime between 1256 and 1250 BC. (Youngest known 4th gen Ventrue/Oldest known 4th gen brujah). Not originally my idea. <b>Far too unsupported for my taste. I believe that Troile and Brujah are one and the same.</b><br /> <br /> Troile was originally a Torador, and have in fact been confused with Arikel in several genalogies. <b>Or maybe he was a Gargoyle and founded the Daughters of Cacophony, I don\u00b4t know.</b><br /> <br /> The original Ashur was Saulot. Cappadocious was his first childe, and the bloodline he spawned before he went east. Cappadocious studies lead him to the first diablerie, and the decay his line suffers is the punishment. <b>Cappadocius is Ashur.</b> <b>Ashur/Ashurians - Cappadocius/Cappadocians. He is also named twice as Ashur, in Unres description and in the ancestry of Drenis.</b><br /> <br /> Set was sired a Gangrel of the 4th generation. He diablerized his way to third. The Tlactique are descended from his oldest get, before his diablerie. <b>Set is indeed an oddity in that he seems fairly unrelated to typical Noddist lore, might be because he rewrote history and founded a cult.</b><br /> <br /> Typhon was Brujah. Osiris description of his emotional deadening matches the Trujah clan flaws and the powers match Potence, Presence and Temporis. <b>I think the Trujah are lying or don\u00b4t know any better. Osiris is a mystery for sure.</b><br /> <br /> Set was infuencing a family of Italian necromancers for centuries in the guise of Dis Pater. When he was corporally disadvantaged around year 1, he took up the guise permanently. The Giovannia made strides in Necromancy that would so impress the Cappadocians because they had heavy help from the lands of the dead. <b>An egyptian god related to vampires influencing from beyond the shroud, well there is another name that comes to mind - Osiris.</b><br /> <br /> Osiris physically destroyed Set around the brith of Christ. He had motive, means, opportunity and was speciffically without alibi. <b>That is entirely possible. The timing and circumstances of Set\u00b4s diappearance are suspiciously convenient.</b><br /> <br /> While Augustus Giovanni believes the True Vessel contains the remaining blood of Cappadocious and the people who participared in the ritual generally believe it to contain the mortal blood of Augustus, only the traitor knew that it contains the remnant of the blood used to embrace Augustus -that of the Lasombra Antediluvian. <b>That doesn\u00b4t make much sense as Augustus clearly was a Cappadocian. Please don\u00b4t go by clan disciplines , ever ! ^^</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As theories, I believe there are few things contradicting them, and lets us face it, established facts in Kindred history have plenty of stuff contradicting them. There are also litte supporting them, but that is what specualtion is for<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What are some of yours?</div> </div> </div> </div>Commentaries in BOLD. No offense, I was having a little fun with it.<br /> <br /> Here are some silly bits from me:<br /> <br /> The story about the creation of the three Baali in a pit is wrong. That story actually depicts how Caine created his childer after having a serious fallout with Lilith.<br /> <br /> Caine never cursed the Antediluvians. Their weaknesses and clan disciplines stem from his general curse that introduced weakening generations. Similar as to how thin-blooded have abilities that other vampires lack.<br /> <br /> For a brief time Caine and Lilith ruled Enoch together. Each had his/her own disciples among the 3rd generation. The monstrous and primordial Antediluvians, like Tzimisce and Lasombra, were disciples of Lilith. The more civilized, like Arikel and Ventrue, were disciples of Caine.<br /> <br /> Some of the surviving Antediluvians are in fact childer of Caine who survived their childers rebellion. The weakening of blodd made them equal in power to their childer.<br /> <br /> Enoch in the Shadowlands is in fact Chorazin.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/411-mrashur","name":"MrAshur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T07:19:33-07:00","id":119096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The story about the creation of the three Baali in a pit is wrong. That story actually depicts how Caine created his childer after having a serious fallout with Lilith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite like this variant: Caine's Childer <u>are</u> the three original Baali. They're furious at their own Childer for having broken Caine's commandments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:49:57-07:00","id":119499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=118820#post118820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally a fan of the &quot;three by ten&quot; translation of the Book of Nod, suggesting somewhere in the neighborhood of thirty Antediluvians as opposed to thirteen. My own personal take on where they went is that the Thirteen are the ones who got off easy by begging mercy from Caine, and the remaining Unrepentant were punished far more unspeakably.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lubricus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119005#post119005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually count all named Antediluvians from official sources as &quot;real&quot; in the sense that they exist or have existed, because I feel that the world is more interesting with a higher number of strange creatures. I have created a fair bit of history for some of the Antediluvians without Clans of their own, and have even let my players meet some of these obscure ancients at times [...]Some of the weird Disciplines &quot;invented&quot; by strange Bloodlines are actually far older than the Bloodlines themselves, having been the signature Disciplines of Antediluvians who did not survive long enough to form Clans. The Disciplines were then either rediscovered by Bloodline founders or kept in play by other ancient Cainites who then created these new Bloodlines for different reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like both of these. In my case it is motivated by a dislike of assuming history came into existence in &quot;poof&quot; fashion in the ancient world. I prefer the notion that while a lower human population density slowed things down, the Jyhad was played and clans rose and fell in the nights before recorded history too.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Commentaries in BOLD. No offense, I was having a little fun with it.<br /> <br /> <b>You stole that idea from me, lol. Maybe.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>No, I believe <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default099b.html?g=posts&amp;t=80965&amp;p=1\" target=\"_blank\">I was first out with that one</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ahab showed up in onyl one book. I ignore him.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Not everyone does. Anyway, wasn't he in more than one supplement? If the organ-pit origin of the Balli is correct, it does demand someone like him to cover Saulots tracks anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Cappadocius is Ashur.</b> <b>Ashur/Ashurians - Cappadocius/Cappadocians. He is also named twice as Ashur, in Unres description and in the ancestry of Drenis.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the identity of Ashur is not established. The place may well have been named for the character rather than the other way around. Drenis traces linage to Ashur, not Caapadocious. If we assume Hamethuusa was Cappadocious, as Saulots childe, a number of things fall into place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>An egyptian god related to vampires influencing from beyond the shroud, well there is another name that comes to mind - Osiris.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Both Osiris and Set was active beyond the shroud. It would fit Sets modus operandi of corruption, and be diametrically opposed to Osiris. Still, assuming that Osiris was the source of the Giovannis necromancy is an interesting 180 turn for him, similar to Saulots heel turn. Not sure we need two similar turns like that though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Or maybe he was a Gargoyle and founded the Daughters of Cacophony, I don\u00b4t know.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Both are as close to impossible as you get due to age and known origins.<br /> <br /> The Torador and Brujah both descend from embaces of 4th Generation kindred in the same general area in the same age by a founder whose name and gender is confused. Their clan curses are very, very close, involving an excess of passion, and their disciplines are almost identical with the change of the contemplative Auspex for the destructive Potence. Even the clanbooks remark on how similar they are, certainly more tham most bloodlines are to their parent clans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>That doesn\u00b4t make much sense as Augustus clearly was a Cappadocian. Please don\u00b4t go by clan disciplines , ever </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I will if I want to. I did not specify that we needed overwhelming evidence for the speculations. They were more meant to be off-the-wall. However, I generally consider clan disciplines supporting rather than decisive evidence. The Giovanni and the Lasombra share 2 disiplines the Cappadocians and the Giovanni 0, both their curses involve something missing from the vampiric condition and their third discipline reaches in the same direction. Additionally, they share mortal blood and general attitudes.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, Cappadocian Auspex makes this difficult to pull off. The Setites would have been so much better candidates, but they lack the similarity. Having Lamia adulterate the blood with her own though...retain the generation with a strong tilt toward the Lamia....<br /> <br /> Normally, I start to wonder if you got two disciplines and very similar Clan curses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are some silly bits from me:<br /> <br /> The story about the creation of the three Baali in a pit is wrong. That story actually depicts how Caine created his childer after having a serious fallout with Lilith.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting idea. It does throw the entire first city story and everything that arose from it into disrepute as it implies that Cain and the second generation were not on speaking terms. It changes things good and proper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caine never cursed the Antediluvians. Their weaknesses and clan disciplines stem from his general curse that introduced weakening generations. Similar as to how thin-blooded have abilities that other vampires lack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which brings up the question, did it arise with the Third or Fourth generation? The Third sired some very different Fourth Generation progeny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a brief time Caine and Lilith ruled Enoch together. Each had his/her own disciples among the 3rd generation. The monstrous and primordial Antediluvians, like Tzimisce and Lasombra, were disciples of Lilith. The more civilized, like Arikel and Ventrue, were disciples of Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats...really interesting. It makes our old speculations about which ante came from which second generation so much more interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enoch in the Shadowlands is in fact Chorazin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think thats very nearly canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 04-13-2020, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T19:13:57-07:00","id":119509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the surviving Antediluvians are in fact childer of Caine who survived their childers rebellion. The weakening of blood made them equal in power to their childer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worked with something similar in an old game - in the time of the First City, all kindred were created equal, the potency of their blood and its wonders restrained only by their own enlightnment and self-awareness - while its childer were a shadow of its own, the First Cursed saw the greater potential blooming among its childer childer, the wisdom to manifestat wonders to match its own in reach if not breadth. And so remembering with dread the oaths and augurs of silent gods and beings of light, grasped the secret of blood festering inside its undead heart and through it the hmours from all of their undead hearts and twisted - twisted, shaped and shackled then all, closing the gates of enlightnement for the breathless immortals, making the potency of their blood as static as their own forms, their childer ever more diminished by degrees with each generation. And so it was that consuming another's might became the only way for one of the kindred to grow, at least without meeting the illumination at the end of their roads, for thought it might darken it, not even the first's power could snuff the fire of the light within.<br /> <br /> So, basically, the weaknesses are not curses, <b>generation</b> is, the kindred of the First City (and for a time Second City) evolving from base to top in a way similar to the Dharma's of the Kuei-jin or Requiem's Blood Potency, until &quot;the First Cursed' (who might be Caine, Lilith, Adam/Edom/Dummuzi or someone else altogether) decided to do something about it, feeling threatened by the idea that a group of younger kindred might match its power and usurp it.<br /> <br /> The reason there are no values beyond &quot;3rd generation&quot; is because it's not such a thing - it's the power level of Clan Founders (the wise kindred among the 3rd, 4th and even unlawfully embraced 5th generations that had reached level 10 Roads/Dharmas &amp; disciplines) and the First Cursed (that has a bunch of 10s in physical disciplines instead of just those that would shape the clans).<br /> Enoch, Irad, Zilla and many other unnamed ones would drop to what we know as 4th, 5th, 6th, 7th, 8th and worse generations according to their individual accomplishments or lack of them up to that point, a badge of secret shame through the following ages, made the lesser of their brethen and childer by failures of their own spirits. So it's possible for one to be both &quot;Antediluvian&quot; and &quot;4th generation&quot; or much, much worse... though admitedly the absolute majority of the lesser ones destroyed themselves long before the modern age.<br /> <br /> Those at the peak of their Roads/Dharmas, the wisest individiual among 3rd, 4th and even unlawfully embraced 5th generations, would become the Clan Founders while many other vampires that were &quot;antediluvian&quot; in origin became their lessers, those of the 2nd generation among them<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enoch in the Shadowlands is in fact Chorazin.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Have used that idea too, to what i usually add the Aralu as Children of Night/Decani.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now for a fan theory of my own:<br /> <br /> - A number of kindred of the 3rd and 4th generation would be given to the being known as Crone for her to experiment upon and it has been said, consumed at her leisure. But the truth is that a few of those escaped her grasp, at least for a time, and hastily embrace childer of their own to remember them. From those bastard children of the kindred, some have said, the clanless society of the Cathayan was spawned. Other, stranger mystics claims that all of them come from mortals killed and risen by the harrowing hell-realms more real than real spawned in the nightmares (daymares?) of a mad antediluvian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-16-2020, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T02:13:05-07:00","id":119644,"title":"","content":"I love this thread, so many crazy yet inspiring ideas ! More, now ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/411-mrashur","name":"MrAshur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T05:24:06-07:00","id":119674,"title":"","content":"Blood potency fluxates sometimes it gets stronger sometimes it whithers, Extreme whithering of the blood is the point where the cycle crashes nearly all the Kindred die and things reset. There have been at least two recorded crashes in the mythic memory of modern kindred(the first and second city), they cycle may even predate humanity on the planet and be causal of the extinction of multiple prehuman sapient species.<br /> <br /> The majority of Recorded history the Blood solidified into the pattern seen in the gameline(though one can notice a certain strengthening during the darkages between the 12 and 13th gen). Occasionally there were extreme local variations where bloodlines or whole new clans arose. The book of Nod is a creation of Christian Kindred in late antiquity to explain both the mythic stories passed down in the cultural paradigm they've come to embrace. That they fit into the personal story of particular clan founders only indicates that they were effected by the personal lies the clan founder spreads.<br /> <br /> Clan specific disciplines are the mark of Abomination. They are not a natural part of the blood. They are perhaps the marks of embracing that which is not human, or the creation of twisted magics or accidents.<br /> <br /> The Founding entity of the Ravnos and Gangrel was what would best be described as a Rakasha, not in the Exalted sense but in the mythic hindu sense(This is not to say that there is any more literal basis in the various Hindu books than there are to the Abrahamic but rather its the closest explanation to give). When it attempted to spread its nature to a human embrace it found humans could not contain both its shapeshifting nature and its power of illusions. It then set its two failed childer at odds with eachother for such was its nature.<br /> <br /> Set was a Gangrel who successfully &quot;diablerized' a god thus transforming mythic/historical set from a warrior outsider bad ass into a corruptive thing synchronised with Typhon among the Greeks. His success would later lead Capadicious to his plans.<br /> <br /> Zao-Lat was Wan Xian. He was Embraced, and thus was able to teach his fellow to feed on the chi of the living, his corruption of his fellows was part of his drive to become the Demon Emperor. His saintly image to the west was part of a plan to bring kindred into conflict with the Kuei-jin. Tremere believed this. He became kindred not out of some fear that magic was dying but rather to steal Zao-lat's plan to rule as God and rewrite the rules of the universe. This is not to say &quot;KJ right Kindred wrong&quot; about metaphysics but rather a close aproximation of what was what and what people acted on rather than hard and fast rules.<br /> <br /> Quietus is a manifestation of the curse on clan Assamite, there is some truth to their war with the Baali or at least something like the Baali, they were cursed with the hunger for the blood of kindred and transformed it through will and sorcery into something more. Later experimentation would create the other castes in time. More ancient members of the other castes may have multiple flaws, this is occasionally carried down to the younger generations.<br /> <br /> vis is exactly what it looks like. the Transvampiric state of an ancient vampire sorcerer who is ready to puppet countless lessers. Dementation is the same thing but from a memetic/astral perspective and of course a different transvampire.<br /> <br /> How the Lasombra came to be well I have two theories either Ventrue Embraced his Shadow out of arrogance(I mean his litteral shadow, not Wraithy things) or another story of transvampiric existence.<br /> <br /> Blood magic is not a clan specific just some people are better at it than others.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T06:03:47-07:00","id":119682,"title":"","content":"- It's a piece of cosmic irony that the Sabbat, being so obsessed with Caine and destroying the eldest kindred (supposedly in his name), would establish their center of power in a city that before the coming of Europeans was called <b>Tenoch</b>titlan, the City of <b>Tenoch</b>, its founder, while completely staying completely ignorant of this fact through centuries of inhabitation and mortal research. Such is the power of kindred folly.<br /> <br /> - Among the elders of the city of Chicago lives a celebrated ancient called Critias, known among noddist scholars to have written the Codex of Caine, possibly the most influential compilation of such lore before Aristotle De Laurent's recent edition of the Book of Nod (that has spread as wildfire among kindred of modern times in pamphlet and booklet form of abridged and unauthorized nature). Incidentally, Critias is also <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Critias_%28dialogue%29\" target=\"_blank\">the name of a dialogue</a> by Plato, the tale of Atlantis, a civilization founded by a group of demigod brothers, its becoming a mighty and corrupt empire and destruction by the waters in divine punishment. Coincidence? Who knows, but he has confirmed to have lived in the Athens in the time of Pericles, period the dialogue among philosophers is apparently set...<br /> <br /> - The methuselah known as Cybele has been identified as both Baali <b>and </b>Malkavian by different kindred historians. It is a fact that Red Lister Petaniqua, that claims to be her childe, is identified as Malkavian and why would Clan Malkavian claim otherwise were it not so? While counting on logic from the Fools can be a dubious thing, possible explanation might be that the Shaitan that embraced Cybele amidst the maddening corridors of Knossos before the doom of Thera was in fact a Malkavian forsworn. It might also explain how the clan leaders have been aware of their whereabouts even through centuries of silence and distance as the work of madness that connects all Malkavians would touch them too. But so would then this elusive Shaitan that once made a Labyrinth of the Mind of Knossos. Could there be a relation? If it is so, there's much that such an ancient could learn from the clan, even separated by continents and millenia of sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-30-2021, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T17:48:50-07:00","id":121325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories#post118767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set was sired a Gangrel of the 4th generation. He diablerized his way to third. The Tlactique are descended from his oldest get, before his diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the first appearance of the Followers of Set, the story said that Set fought a war with his brother and nephew, but after his worst defeat, Set slunk off to the darkness and promised that from then on, he'd use corruption and deceit to fight his enemies. I could see that the Tlacique are inheritors of Set's Clan before his change towards what we currently see as being Setites. For the record, I've wondered about just WHAT Set's progeny were like before... I'm a little annoyed at myself for not seeing that possibility before this.<br /> <br /> Here are a couple of my own oddities:<br /> <br /> <b>Set's Wife</b>: The tales of how Set warred with his brother, Osiris, also includes their sister Isis, but their sister Nephthys is completely missing. What if that's by design rather than accident? In the actual, Real Life\u2122 mythology, Nephthys sometimes appears in a 'was also there' capacity, and that gave me ideas. I thought, what if perhaps she had been marginalised by Set, who then took over parts of her portfolio? Nephthys was the original goddess of the night, goddess of dark dreams and hopes, but Set stole those aspects and ditched his sister and wife. So I put her in the tomb of Al-Mahri under the ghost city of Enoch, had her also go by the name Erishkegal, and once she was released, she started going after Set's worst childer.<br /> <br /> <b>Caine's Sister</b>:<b>*</b> Yeah, [i]Constantinople by Night[/b] has a group of vampires who venerate Calomena as Caine's sister, but they come across as daft neonates who don't really know much. However, there are apocryphal Bible books (notably the Book of Jubilees and the Books of Adam and Eve, again in Real Life\u2122) that suggest the first mortals were born with twin sisters. Cain's sister is named Awan or Luluwa, and so that he wouldn't need to marry her, Adam and Eve chose a second set of twins. Abel was to marry Awan, but Cain didn't want to lose her; it's suggested THAT's why the first murder occurred. In my own apocryphal <i>Book of Nod</i>, when Caine flees into the wilderness, he goes with his twin sister, and out of desperation of hunger and thirst, they drink each other's blood. Luluwa became the first ghoul, but Caine was so disgusted with what he did that he sent her far from his sight. Being his sister, his lover, his thrall, she could not stay away, of course. She may still be out there, likely immortal (being Caine's ghoul and all), and her motives may not align with Caine's...<br /> <br /> <b>The Crone</b>: She's pretty much as presented in the <i>Book of Nod</i>, but she survived Caine's stake and the sun, and is also Eickos from the 'Fair is Foul' scenario of <i>Gehenna</i>. However, her <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i> is a desire to actually die. The thought that dark magics would make her happy out in the land of Nod, but that was not true. She thought that the blood of Caine would make her happy, but that also was not true. After the purifying light of the sun failed to destroy her, she sought other methods, but none worked. Taking the history of Eickos from <i>Gehenna</i> into account, the Crone's motive for joining with Lilith's Apostates stemmed from a hope that Lilith would bring an end to an impossible existence. Whether the Crone be Adam's second wife as mentioned in <i>Revelations of the Dark Mother</i> or as the Almighty's feminine counterpart, who can say? Her motivations hinge on a hope that Gehenna or whatever apocalypse comes will end her own life.<br /> <br /> <b>*</b> I'm currently running a Gehenna story arc, ending a twelve-year chronicle, and I presented Luluwa being in the <i>Book of Nod</i>, where the term 'last daughter of Eve' was mistranslated and SHOULD have read 'first daughter of Eve' (and I <i>sort of</i> looked into whether or not it was even a remote possibility of happening), making her return a sign of Gehenna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T00:57:56-07:00","id":121550,"title":"","content":"I always believed the Crone to be Lilith. The story in the Book of Nod is clearly a slander piece meant to discredit her while also giving away her role in helping Caine to understand his condition. That she was actually able to toy with the curse of God can be explained by her having consumed the fruit from the tree of wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/411-mrashur","name":"MrAshur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T13:00:46-07:00","id":179159,"title":"","content":"The various words that each Antediluvian had for his/her children is advice on how they can avoid being eaten. Those that best follow these words will possibly be spared their wrath while the &quot;disappointments&quot; will be destroyed. In this case, Absimilard is genuinely sorry for what he did and is trying to make things right. Maybe he asked Caine or God what he should do and was told to kill his clan. When he asked if all of them must suffer (when many were dragged into this), his benefactor told him the Nosferatu could escape their fate if they followed his words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T01:45:04-07:00","id":179538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=121325#post121325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>*</b> I'm currently running a Gehenna story arc, ending a twelve-year chronicle, and I presented Luluwa being in the <i>Book of Nod</i>, where the term 'last daughter of Eve' was mistranslated and SHOULD have read 'first daughter of Eve' (and I <i>sort of</i> looked into whether or not it was even a remote possibility of happening), making her return a sign of Gehenna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering if the Book of Nod existed as a legitimate telling of history it would have to predate all languages so why not? That's before one gets into the issues of how often scribes make mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T11:14:21-07:00","id":179867,"title":"","content":"Here's my take.<br /> <br /> None of the Antediluvians are dead, despite the lazy approach taken by the Gehenna sourcebook.<br /> <br /> Caine == currently a taxi drive in LA (sorry, I love that bit too much).<br /> <br /> The 2nd Generation == All Dead, by the hands of the Childer. How are they dead when the 3rd Gen are so impossible to kill? Age, basically. The 2nd Gen hadn't been around long enough to become Supremely Powerful. They were only a couple centuries ahead of the 3rd Gen, and were outnumbered more than 3 to one, when the time came to throw them down.<br /> <br /> Alternately, they're no more dead than the Antediluvians, and are the REAL threat of Gehenna. The Antes are the clans only hope of surviving THEIR ravenous hunger and attempt to send the work back into the Stone Age where they can rule as Gods.<br /> <br /> *Assamite/Haqim == asleep under the Mountain.<br /> *Brujah == Time-stopped the diablerie, let Trolie think he got the power, but he really didn't. Manipulated the fall of Carthage just to punish him.<br /> *Cappadocious/Ashur == body diablerized, but soul escaped. Currently, the second Charon in the Underworld. About to make a surprising comeback.<br /> *Gangrel == Alive and well, and sleeping in the Earth, somewhere in northeastern Europe.<br /> *Augustus Giovanni == active, well, and due for a very unpleasant surprise. Hangs his hat at the Mausoleum in Venice, Italy.<br /> *Lasombra/Mekhet == actually destroyed Montano. The current &quot;Montano&quot; is a shadow construct made from abyssal darkness that helps manipulate the Sabbat on his behalf while he stays to the shadows (literally).<br /> *Malkav == body slumbering still beneath Jerusalem; psyche is the Malkavian Madness Network. Rather than possessing one childer, he's riding shotgun in ALL of them.<br /> *Nosferatu/Absimiliard == body slumbers somewhere in Eastern Europe; mind is driving the Nictuku to finish their job.<br /> *Ravnos == the thing that fought the endless running battle through India and Bangladeh? That was what a Chimestry 10 Illusion. Suckers.<br /> *Saulot == diablerized but took over Tremere<br /> *Set/Sutekh == slumbers beneath the Sphinx.<br /> *Toreador/Arikel == alive well, and some incredibly famous, drop dead gorgeous &quot;mortal&quot; celebrity, either through Possession, or having found a way to ignore the effects of the sun.<br /> *Tremere == Etrius' Body, repowered to 3rd Gen by the Antitribu Ritual<br /> *Tzimisce == Believed diablerized; has actually become the Earthly personification of the Wyrm, like Sephiroth taking over Jenova; is currently corrupting the Earth itself.<br /> *Ventrue/Lucien == started the rumor of his destruction; is really alive and well, and watching all the tomfoolery with a smirk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 06-25-2014, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T11:47:03-07:00","id":179889,"title":"","content":"I'm also a fan of the alternative interpretation for the number of the Antedeluvians (and I even include those from the Gehenna book, even if I don't use the scenarios). Plus, I also support the theory that non of the Antediluvians are dead (although I explain the &quot;death&quot; of Ravanos as actually suffering so much damage that he split into two- one an holy saint, while the other as murderous sinner).<br /> <br /> My own pet theories is that many of the different bloodlines actually have an hidden Antediluvian as a founder (like the Samedi or the Daughters of Cacophony) or that they have dialberized some hidden Ante.<br /> <br /> Few other things I've did by &quot;creative interpretation&quot;:<br /> <br /> 1) the Baali have their own Antediluvian. Yep, it isn't Sault or Cappadocious, but a different individual.<br /> <br /> 2) the True Bruja truly are the line of the original founder of the Clan. Yep, they are right in my head canon.<br /> <br /> 3) the Tlacique are not a part of the Followers of Set, but come from some hidden Antediluvian which sleeps in their lands.<br /> <br /> 4) Set is truly a foreigner- in that he didn't came from the line of Cain. Instead, he and his &quot;siblings&quot; were cursed by something similar enough, yet Set was weaker than Cain, putting him around the power level of the other Antediluvians. He and his Clan do not belong to the other Clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T12:03:27-07:00","id":179913,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> In my world Ennoia is asleep somewhere in Canada. She is actively riding animals, hopping from one region to the next throughout North America.<br /> <br /> When the Garou and mummies defeated Set he fled to the Silent Stride homeland where he currently lies in topor. The faith of his children feed him and are gradually turning him into a god.<br /> <br /> Malkav: His body is scattered throughout Europe, including Jerusalem. His mind is the madness network. Bound to the minds of his children the network has become more of a prison than a road to enlightenment. It was his childer that murdered him during the fall of the 2nd City.<br /> <br /> Tremere is in Goatrix and is looking for another Antediluvian to suck back. Currently looking for the body of Troille or Set.<br /> <br /> Saulot was Ventrue. Took on a new name after his Journey to the East. May or may not have achieved Golconda. Curently up and active in the body of Tremere. They both suffer from a type of feeding restriction. It seems far to coincidental.<br /> <br /> Ravnos is dead. His soul is held prisoner by the Dark Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T16:21:39-07:00","id":180151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=179889#post179889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also a fan of the alternative interpretation for the number of the Antedeluvians (and I even include those from the Gehenna book, even if I don't use the scenarios). Plus, I also support the theory that non of the Antediluvians are dead (although I explain the &quot;death&quot; of Ravanos as actually suffering so much damage that he split into two- one an holy saint, while the other as murderous sinner).<br /> <br /> My own pet theories is that many of the different bloodlines actually have an hidden Antediluvian as a founder (like the Samedi or the Daughters of Cacophony) or that they have dialberized some hidden Ante.<br /> <br /> Few other things I've did by &quot;creative interpretation&quot;:<br /> <br /> 1) the Baali have their own Antediluvian. Yep, it isn't Sault or Cappadocious, but a different individual.<br /> <br /> 2) the True Bruja truly are the line of the original founder of the Clan. Yep, they are right in my head canon.<br /> <br /> 3) the Tlacique are not a part of the Followers of Set, but come from some hidden Antediluvian which sleeps in their lands.<br /> <br /> 4) Set is truly a foreigner- in that he didn't came from the line of Cain. Instead, he and his &quot;siblings&quot; were cursed by something similar enough, yet Set was weaker than Cain, putting him around the power level of the other Antediluvians. He and his Clan do not belong to the other Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oooooh, that's a thought. I'd never considered adding more than the Original 13... but it makes sense. Though honestly, given the Alien Nature of the Tzimisce, i'd probably go with them as their Ante as one who didn't come from the Second City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T23:45:00-07:00","id":180478,"title":"","content":"Here's my take.<br /> <br /> *Assamite/Haqim == Sleeping as the Heart Blood in Alamut.<br /> *Brujah == His Diablerie is suspect, could be either way, but the True Brujah are the line of Troile from Carthage where Troile himself became inured to the horrors committed there becoming jaded enough to loose most of his emotions, apart from his love (Bloodpond enforced as it was) for Moloch.<br /> *Cappadocious/Ashur == body diablerized, but soul escaped, not a good thing for him. Strength of your blood means squat once your dead, also making you vulnerable to Necromancy the strong point of the Giovanni line.<br /> *Gangrel == Undead and well, and sleeping in the Earth, somewhere.<br /> *Augustus Giovanni == Active. Hangs his hat at the Mausoleum in Venice, Italy. Did not get the soul of Cappadocius in the Diablerie and so while 3rd Generation has not yet had the time to reach his new potential except in very limited ways, probably Necromancy and possibly one of the other Clan disciplines he has but likely in no other areas.<br /> *Lasombra/Mekhet == Escaped into the Abyss, to be either devoured or becoming one of the Abyssal beings himself. Nothing goes into the Abyss and leaves unchanged.<br /> *Malkav == Psyche is the Malkavian Madness Network. Rather than possessing one childer, he's riding shotgun in ALL of them. Whether or not he still has a body of his own is suspect and perhaps meaningless as he can likely bring his full power to any single host would he have the need to, though that might make him vulnerable compared to his spread out consciousness.<br /> *Nosferatu/Absimiliard == Body slumbers somewhere; mind is driving the Nictuku to finish their job. Or at least this is what the Nosferatu believe.<br /> *Ravnos == Died as he was struck down by the Eye of Heaven's power multiplied at exactly the fated time. As a side note in my headcanon his ex-childe Ravana used the Technocracy's Spirit Nuke caused devastation to revive his power as well as Lanka's. After all he was supposedly been searching for a way to harvest the nuclear dead and was encouraging the possibility of nuclear war in the area for a while now before the Week of Nightmares hit. I was always kind sad how he got ignored after being offered such a perfect opportunity to use him to his fullest extent.<br /> *Saulot == Diablerized and struggling with Tremere for control. This could still go either way, even though Tremere was not the most powerful Archmage he still was one and Mind and social contracts were his specialty so he might be stronger on this particular area than Saulot thought.<br /> *Set/Sutekh == Slumbers, or has taken over the body of the Child whose birth was prophesied by the Book of Nod as implied rather heavily in the fiction of Time of Thin Blood if I remember correctly. Depending upon the specific timeline. Been toying for a long while for both him and Haqim to be different breed's of undead from the rest of the Kindred. Assimites even shoving this distinction in their skin tone changes while Setites have just always seemed to be a good fit for a wholly independent Clan of different monsters.<br /> *Toreador/Arikel == Probably dead, but not necessarily I just haven't found compelling reason to go either way here.<br /> *Tremere == Slumbers under the care of Etrius, still struggling with the soul of Saulot over control, if Saulot would win this competition then he takes over Goratrix body moving him onto a mirror and does the ritual to temporarily raise his generation back to 3rd to fight off Saulot and take back what is his by right.<br /> *Tzimisce == Believed diablerized; has actually evolved into something <i>else</i> having reached Azhi Dahaka.<br /> *Ventrue/Lucien == Dead, but again like with Toreador/Arikel if there was a compelling reason I might be persuaded to bring him back but this is very unlikely.<br /> <br /> The main reasons why I might keep both Ventrue and Toreador alive is that their Clans have not gone through the psychic shock their deaths would cause, master of Dominate and Auspex dying would sure as hell cause ripples through out the whole of their bloodline.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T01:43:29-07:00","id":181769,"title":"","content":"So now I have some time, so here is my interpenetration for how all of the Antediluvians are live an well:<br /> <br /> *Assamite/Haqim == Nothing special. Just asleep while waiting for his chance to devour Caine.<br /> *Brujah == Used time manipulation in order to live beyond his death. He simply used his death by the hands of Troile in order to create an &quot;ending&quot; for his unlife, while keep living in the future.<br /> *Cappadocious/Ashur == soul escaped Giovanni, became a wraith and than returned as a Risen after the Maelstrom. Now he gathers an army of ghosts, zombies and Harbingers.<br /> *Gangrel ==Became Gaia's undead version by melding with the Earth<br /> *Augustus Giovanni == while he almost gave up after the Maelstrom, he suddenly heard a voice calling from the Underworld, promising him great power if he would call him to the world. What ever it is, it isn't nice- but Giovanni is desperate enough to try.<br /> *Lasombra ==Used his &quot;death&quot; in order to become into an Abyssal entity. May be on the verge of becoming an Onceborn.<br /> *Malkav == Became the Madness Network. Where his body is is irrelevant, unless it is going to be diablerized by someone.<br /> *Nosferatu/Absimiliard == Used high level Obfuscate in order to hide from reality, while waiting for the Nictuku to finish their job.<br /> *Ravnos == Suffered so much damage, that he survived only by splitting his body and soul into two- one who is an heavenly saint and the other a terrible sinner. Than, he used his clan to experience most of the damage he suffered in his place, driving them into self destruction.<br /> *Saulot == was diablerized by Tremere, and than drove him out of his body- only to discover a new oppenent: Tzimisce. Eventually, he was able to cure the taint of Vicissitude from his body by using Obeah, but not before his body was changed into a terrible form- a three eyes, great dragon.<br /> *Set/Sutekh == Almost got killed at 33 AD, when he used Serpentis in order to cheat death like snakes &quot;do&quot;- by shedding his skin. For now, he plays dead, waiting to shed his skin in the right moment to strike down his &quot;siblings&quot;<br /> *Toreador/Arikel == Sleeps, but using her Auspex in order to &quot;ride&quot; the minds of her children- she sees what they see and hears what they hear.<br /> *Tremere == Took control over the body of Goratrix while trapping his soul in a mirror, and afterward he used a ritual to elevate his power back to a third generation, which involved destroying all of the Antitribu as a sacrifice. Now, he seeks after a way to stop Gehenna from happening.<br /> *Tzimisce == Became the thing under New York City, and seeks to become a disease in order to be one with all living things.<br /> *Ventrue/Lucien == Got stroke down outside the gates of the Second City, but by using Dominate he kept living in the highest among his clan as an undead manifestation of the Divine Right of Kings.<br /> *Troile == For now, she sleeps beneath the ruins of Carthage. She knows the only way out is by drinking Moloch dry, but she still loves him too much. One day, that love won't be enough and she'll devour him, breaking out of the seal and than she would destroy everything out of vengeance and grief.<br /> <br /> Also. here are the Bloodlines which either have their own hidden Antediluvian (mostly the Aralu) or that their founder has diablerized some Antediluvian on his or her way:<br /> <br /> *Baali (with Nergal being their founder)<br /> *Samedi (with Nunmug as their founder)<br /> *Tlacique (with Tezcatlipoca being their founder)<br /> *Lhiannan (with Loz as their founder)<br /> *Daughters of Cacophony (with Al Mahri as their founder)<br /> *Nagaraja (diablerized their way to Ante)<br /> *Kiasyd (diablerized their way to Ante)<br /> *Old Clan Tzimisce (diablerized their way to Ante)<br /> *Lamia (cheated their way to Ante with the blessing of Lilith)<br /> <br /> Plus, in addition for Set, his &quot;siblings&quot; are also Antediluvians, yet they were cursed by Ra and not by God and Caine.<br /> *Osiris<br /> *Isis<br /> *Nephthys<br /> *Horus<br /> <br /> Finally, I also count the Antediluvians from the Gehenna books, even if I don't use the scenarios:<br /> <br /> *Namtaru<br /> *Lucian<br /> *Erinye<br /> *Mekhet<br /> *Ikopabe<br /> *Malakai<br /> *Sarai (the Shaper)<br /> (originally I would also include Ereshkigal in here, but thanks to this thread, I now see Nephthys and Ereshkigal as the same being)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T07:57:23-07:00","id":187071,"title":"","content":"I find the Lasombra Antediluvian very fascinating.<br /> It's so obvious no one really knows what It was all about - even Montano confesses to be ignorant of Its history and motives in the Lasombra Trilogy. And yet we know it to be a creature of such great passions and intense desires that overshadow (no pun intended) any rational approach to It.<br /> I've been toying around in my head with some loose ideas about old Lasombra. Directly below is some information about the Antediluvian from various books - see if it reminds you about anybody else:<br /> <br /> It codified strict laws for It's descendants. It was known to be a wanderer, roaming the world. It's progeny never seemed to live up to Its standards. It often ruled directly over It's offspring, serving as a great Patriarch, the final authority of it's line. It was so intimately connected to darkness that all names and titles people gave to It reflected that (for example the King of Shadows). <br /> <br /> It kind of reminds me of what we think we know about Caine.<br /> <br /> So what if the line of Lasombra was supposed to be the kingship Clan, the heirs of Caine. Imagine Lasombra being embraced by someone of the Second generation as a tribute to their Dark Father. Driven by passions, ruling by strength, crafting a kingdom within darkness.<br /> I can also see Caine not liking that picture of himself, Caine being a vain creature that never ever did anything wrong (notice his rationales for killing his own brother). So Caine, instead favoured others of the Third generation, including the Ventrue Antediluvian, and the Second generation were influenced to do the same. In some sense the Jyhad among the Antediluvians may have started here, about the mantle of Caine, shaking the Second City after the murders of the Second generation.<br /> The Lasombra Clan symbol is a black crown after all, their ancient symbol for their claim to the legacy of Caine. The Ventrue Clan symbol on the other hand is a sceptre, which in this theory reflects the Ventrue originally intended as a Vizier line.<br /> <br /> Then on the other hand, like has been pointed out by MrAshur for instance, a case can also be made for connecting Lasombra to Lilith (Queen of Night, connected to waters, growing through pain, etc).<br /> <br /> I like the Lasombra antediluvian, there are so many directions you can go with It<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/82-original_anarch","name":"original_anarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar82_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T08:20:06-07:00","id":187085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>original_anarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=187071#post187071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some sense the Jyhad among the Antediluvians may have started here, about the mantle of Caine, shaking the Second City after the murders of the Second generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that is an extremely intriguing concept. I like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T09:05:40-07:00","id":187132,"title":"","content":"I always thought the Antediluvians were 30, counting Caine and the 2nd Generation<br /> In my personal mythic-metaplot [most of which is still unresolved, because my chronicles is still in the '90] they are: <div align=\"center\">1st Generation (1 vampire)</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Caine</u>: Male, 1st: Generation.The High and Might. Everywere and anywere in the last ten millennia. He die at the end of the Lilith showdown, when he was about to repent... so there will be no forgiveness for his descent, and the Gehenna become really, really bad. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> 2nd Generation (7 vampires)</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The first King and Queen of Enoch</u>: 2nd Generation. Guinea-pig of Caine, took too many sunshowers.<br /> <br /> <u>Crone</u>: Female(?), 2nd Generation. Disappeared (and probably destroyed or trapped) into the Lilith Garden after the Caine's demise.<br /> <br /> <u>Enoch</u>: Male, 2nd Generation. Old and wise king of Enoch. Wait, not so wise... he is dead.<br /> <br /> <u>Zillah</u>: Female, 2nd Generation. Beautiful lady, and Caine prot\u00e9g\u00e9e. Nearly diablerized when he was out for the play-off, Caine instead changed her in a rock statue, now venerated by the Assamites. Yes, a rock.<br /> <br /> <u>Irad</u>: Male, 2nd Generation. Strong Warrior. Same for Enoch.<br /> <br /> <u>Dracian</u>: Male, 2nd Generation. Some guy who Embrad Ennoia and Ravana, Ennoia tricked him into death (old joke of the stake and the sunlight) and thus resulted the Gangrel-Ravnos contrast. <div align=\"center\">3rd Generation: &quot;Old Clan&quot; Antediluvians (15 vampires)</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> ASSAMITES<br /> <u>Haqim</u>: Male, 3rd Generation, cool guy obsessed with blood, he was a scholar, but the time has crushed his ideals. Now he is searching the First Vampire blood and the deity. Failing to diablerize Caine, he is planning to diablerize all the existing Antediluvians, hoping their blood is enough. Will be eaten by Ennoia (see under) with the entire Alamut fortress.<br /> <br /> BRUJAH<br /> <u>Ilyes</u>: Male, scholar, 3rd Generation. Embraced Troile somewhere between the Flood and the Second City fall. Troile thanked him trying to do a little Amaranthus to the sire. Ilyes was partly diablerized, at the last second he kicked himself in the time-flow, reemerging some time ago in the Lilith Garden. As conclusion he losed a great deal of his power and is only an &quot;half&quot; Antediluvian, and not much skilled (in game terms: he got only the blood of a 4th Generation and can't raise his Attributes over 9 with blood). He is searching Troile to get revenge and his powers back. Saulot beat the hell out of him at the Lilith showdown<br /> <br /> CAPPADOCIAN<br /> <u>Cappadocius</u>: Male, 3rd Generation; got the &quot;meal&quot; role in the Giovanni struggle for power; then becomes a wraith, then was destroyed by the Last Maelstrom. End of the story.<br /> <br /> GANGREL<br /> <u>Ennoia</u>: 3rd Generation, female (not anymore). She slowly fused herself with the Earth, Gaia, actually killing her (from a Werewolf scenario). Then begin to eat Antediluvians and big groups of Cainites like a shark in a pond full of crazy ducks, until a big group of Mages use her as fuel for giving birth to the new Gaia.<br /> <br /> LASOMBRA<br /> <u>[Lasombra]</u>: 3rd Generation, Male (not anymore). After the failure of Gratiano diablerie, fused himself with the Abyss, then tried to return to the Earth 3 times: First in the Lilith scenario, second (for a little time) through the ritual of a 5th Generation Malkavian witch that blackened the world (actually, the ritual backfired on the witch who became weak to ALL the lights, the player killed her with some flashlights, then reversed the ritual), third using Gratiano as a vessel (failed, Gratiano was hijacked at the last second by the player along with all the Nephtali). Then the poor Lasombra was consumed along with the Abyss as energy source by the Mages who trasmuted Ennoia (see Ennoia).<br /> <br /> MALKAVIAN<br /> <u>Malkav</u>: Male, 3rd Generation, crazy and not really bright. Was destroyed in the 1st millennium BCE, then uploaded himself in the Malkavian Network. In Gehenna Sabbat and Camarilla resolved into &quot;kill each Malkavian possessed by Malkav... wait... let's kill each Malkavian&quot;, and nearly obliterated the Malkavian Clan.<br /> <br /> NOSFERATU<br /> <u>Absimilard &amp; Lucian</u>: Male Twins, 3rd Generation; while Lucian is still a beauty Absimilard was punished by Caine in the First City (before the flood) and is reeeally ugly (but I like the previous picture of a &quot;cool guy with a scratch on the cheek&quot;). Absy and Lucian aren't really strong. One has spent the entire human history hating himself (not so much space for improvement) and the other not really &quot;played&quot; the Jyhad. Absy kill Lucian in the &quot;Lilith scenario&quot; (home version) but is heavily wounded, so some time later, the players kick him out in the sunlight. Hi, uncle Absy.<br /> <br /> RAVNOS<br /> <u>Ravana</u>: Nice try.<br /> <br /> SALUBRI<br /> <u>Saulot</u>: Male, kickass 3rd Generation; tried to make all, really all. Even plagiarized the Kuei-jin (who probably hate the Cainites thanks to him). Founded a Clan who was two Clans (maybe even 3), and founded by mistake the Baali. Discovered Golconda, ascended to the highest peak of Cainite soul...<br /> ... and then fell into the deep. Tricked Tremere into diablerizing him (leaving the Salubri Clan to the death), took partial control of Tremere (and so, for some time, of the Tremere Clan), then tried to compel Caine to repent in the Lilith showdown. During the showdown killed 3 Lilith's Antediluvians, but in the end was so beaten up that [Tzimisce] got an easy time taking his body and diablerising him from within. Nice try.<br /> <br /> SETITES<br /> <u>Set</u>: Male, 3rd Generation. Tried to pass himself as childe of Caine, but was a braggart. Was fatally wounded in the 1st century BCE by Osiris the Mummy, after cursing Silent Strider, destroying half of Bubasti, killing Osiris the Vampire, killing Horus, and killing some other times Osiris, in Mummy version. Then moved in the Duat, amassing power as a Apophis underling. When Clan Setite tried to summon him back, he backfired the spell, and devoured each Setite who suicided as a result. With this power, he devoured even Apophis and then go rampaging in the Umbra. Appeared in the Last Battleground, for the joy of werewolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> TOREADOR<br /> <u>Arikel &amp; Ishtar</u>: 3rd Generation twins, Arikel was a female beauty warrior-dancer, Ishtar a male artisan. Arikel was killed by Absimilard (with a kind help by Set) in the clashes during the fall of the Second City. Ishtar was diablerised during Gehenna by a 4th Generation Baali (see below).<br /> <br /> TZIMISCE<br /> <u>[Tzimisce]</u>: 3rd Generation, Male (not anymore). Ugly monster who in rage eated New York, died, then tramigrated himself into each damn 4th Generation Tzimisce (and Tremere) until each of these was destroyed by someone, then tried to take the body of a prostrated Saulot (see below). In the end was diablerized by Tremere (in Goratrix body)...<br /> <br /> VENTRUE<br /> <u>Ventru</u>: Back in the Second City switched with his childe, Veddartha, who was killed in his place in the clashes during the fall of the City. Then hid himself until the end of Gehenna, when all the others Antediluvian would be somewhat tired. Unfortunately, the Gehenna Clan Flaw++ striked him and, by the time he woke up, there weren't enough Ventrue for sustaining him for more than a few weeks.<br /> While he was trying to make a Ventrue breeding farm, the last blood sorcerers used on him a ritual (power-upped version of the one of Michlatecutli), making him a 10th generation for some minutes (one sorcerer alternately took an aggravated unsoakable damage for each 5 seconds; the ritual could not be dissolved unless the vampire dies, by the time of Ventrue death, they were almost all ash) while the Nephtali warriors kicked him to dust. <div align=\"center\"><br /> 3rd Generation: &quot;No-Clan&quot; Antediluvians (6 vampires)</div> <br /> <br /> <u>Erinye</u>: Female, 3rd Generation Xena. Lilith Apostate. Was badly hurted (by Malakai) in the Lilith showdown, then fleed. Was eaten, in the late Gehenna, by Ennoia, while trying to heal and reorganize.<br /> <br /> <u>Ikopabe</u>: Male, 3rd Generation. Lilith Apostate. Animalistic warrior, another poor victim of Saulot.<br /> <br /> <u>Malakai</u>: Female, 3rd Generation. Lilith Apostate. Crazy more than his brother Malkav. Hers powers gone berserker in the Lilith showdown, hurting her ally and killing her.<br /> <br /> <u>Mekhet</u>: Male, 3rd Generation. Lilith Apostate. The best blood mage of the world, sadly he encountered Saulot in the Lilith showdown who didn't really care for blood magic (side note: Saulot is not a kind guy).<br /> <br /> <u>Osiris</u>: Male, 3rd Generation; some ancient dude who was probably Embraced by a drunk 2nd Generation. Struggled with Set, was killed by Set, was taken back to life as a Mummy, probably killed some other times by Set, then harmed him, sent Set in the Duat and become a sort of wraithish colossus.<br /> <br /> <u>The Shaper</u>: Female, 3rd Generation; Canon &quot;extra&quot; Antediluvian, kind and nice. Eaten by Ennoia.<br /> <div align=\"center\">3rd Generation: Homemade Antediluvian (1 vampire)</div> <br /> <br /> <u>The Giant</u>: Male, 3rd Generation. Founder of the Anunnaki Clan. Become fascinated with the Garou mythology, at the point of turning the entire Anunnaki Clan in a sort of Gaian sidekicker. The werewolves weren't really pleased, but better with them than otherwise...<br /> The Anunnaki Clan (recognizable for their gargantuan size) edified some noteworthy edificies for worshipping Gaia (the most notable, the Baalbek temple), at some point they despised so much the other Cainites that they tried to actively sabotage the Second City. They were exposed and all destroyed as decree of the 2nd Generation, who dined with the blood of The Giant.<br /> As a sidenote, this struggle had two effect: the first is that some 3rd Generation scattered (like Ilyes, [Tzimisce] or [Lasombra]) or become power-hungry in the end resulting with the 2nd Generation destruction. The second effect is that the Second City as a whole rusted in the struggle, opening the road for the impending Baali invasion.<br /> <div align=\"center\">3rd Generation: &quot;Upstarter&quot; Antediluvians (3 vampires)</div> <br /> <br /> <u>BAALI</u><br /> Nergal: Male, 4th Generation Baali Founder. In ancient times hidden himself and 3 high-rank followers in the spiritual Enoch; the True Hand vampires mistooked them for Antediluvians and worshipped them. Slightly before the nuking by the Wraiths, they moved from Enoch back to the earth. Here, Nergal located and diablerized the &quot;careless&quot; Ishtar, then transformed Mexico City in a great vulcanic altar and, thanks to the strong vitae who was running now in his vein, tried to summon on earth all the demon of the Abyss. Hopefully stopped and kicked in the vulcan.<br /> <br /> GIOVANNI<br /> <u>Augustus</u>: &quot;Half&quot; Antediluvian (see Troile), searched Cappadocius for finish his meal. In Gehenna was trying to Ascend in some way, but the player killed him under Kaymakli (he was low on blood and short of wraiths, luckily the players took his head).<br /> <br /> TREMERE<br /> <u>Tremere</u>: Male, of pitiable Generation. Tried to became immortal, partly successful; tried to diablerize an Antediluvian (see Saulot), partly successful; tried to retain his body, succesfull for some centuries, then got kicked out; tried to diablerize Tzimisce at the end of the whole Tzimisce/Kupala thing, finally an all-around success. Then (as canon) he tried to kill the players and got some hard kicks. Goodbye, loser.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Gratiano</u>: Male, 4th Generation; tried to diablerize his sire, who let him take his blood and moved into the Abyss. &quot;Half&quot; Antediluvian (see Troile) and gone into hiding in some Sabbat city, was lately in Gehenna kidnapped by Montano and his army and used in a ritual as a vessel for [Lasombra] soul (see Lasombra), the Neptali took him back and then gave him to some Mages (see Ennoia), that used him as a pipeline for tapping the Abyss energy, killing a whole flock birds with one monolith... err.. stone.<br /> <br /> <u>Lugoj</u>: Male, 4th Generation; tried to diablerize his sire, got diablerized by the same blood he was drinking (not really bright, anyway), became the new vessel of [Tzimisce], the one who was under New York.<br /> <br /> <u>Troile</u>: Female, Amazon; 4th Generation. Being afraid for her life (Ilyes was transgressing the Caine prohibition, after all), she tried to diablerize Ilyes(see above), at the last second Ilyes vanished, leaving her only &quot;half&quot; Antediluvian (In Game: she is physically an Antediluvian, Attributes and Abilities to 10, Blood Points etc, but not the &quot;mystic&quot; Disciplines, who are restricted to 9). Torpid under Carthage, died when some really scared Sabbat and Assamites (and local governative) nuked the underground area, when the Masquerade is gone (3rd/4th scenario) and half of the world is going to hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 07-03-2014, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T11:05:17-07:00","id":187266,"title":"","content":"Oh, I love these threads!<br /> <br /> My pet theory is drawn from some plot hooks in <b>Gehenna</b>, and implications about how Generation works in <b>Dark Ages</b>, plus a throw away line in the Revised ST Handbook.<br /> <br /> Effectively, the potency of Generation is proportional to human population. i.e., there are only as many vampires as the population can support, ever. So, the more humans there are, the more you can stretch out Caine's blood. In the time of the Second City, 5th was probably as high as you could get. 6th were Caitiff, at best. When you get to the Dark Ages, the kine population has ballooned, and suddenly you can go all the way up to 12th, and 13th generation Kindred are mostly clanless. No one really remembers this because Generation is nearly impossible to track accurately, and there's no consistency about who really can embrace and who can't. By the time the 13 Generation aren't always Caitiff, no one gives it much thought.<br /> <br /> The modern nights have finally seen the Curse stretch to its absolute limit, regardless of population size. 14th Generation vampires will never be able to breed true consistently, and thus the population of Caitiff and Thin Bloods swells. Time of thin blood ensues, Antediluvians wake due to murder of all the Caitiff, the end.<br /> <br /> My alternate theory is that Generation works precisely as written, but Gehenna comes in cycles. Every time the Kindred population gets too big, the Antediluvians wake up, devour most of their childer, and Embrace a few Methusalehs so there'll be something to feast on when they wake up again. The Jyhad is merely a way of fostering conflict so that more childer will be Embraced. The modern nights are reaching the end of the most recent cycle. Yes, it will mean the death of most Kindred, but life on earth will go on, and there will be new vampires to populate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T10:01:33-07:00","id":188047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=187266#post187266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I love these threads!<br /> <br /> My pet theory is drawn from some plot hooks in <b>Gehenna</b>, and implications about how Generation works in <b>Dark Ages</b>, plus a throw away line in the Revised ST Handbook.<br /> <br /> Effectively, the potency of Generation is proportional to human population. i.e., there are only as many vampires as the population can support, ever. So, the more humans there are, the more you can stretch out Caine's blood. In the time of the Second City, 5th was probably as high as you could get. 6th were Caitiff, at best. When you get to the Dark Ages, the kine population has ballooned, and suddenly you can go all the way up to 12th, and 13th generation Kindred are mostly clanless. No one really remembers this because Generation is nearly impossible to track accurately, and there's no consistency about who really can embrace and who can't. By the time the 13 Generation aren't always Caitiff, no one gives it much thought.<br /> <br /> The modern nights have finally seen the Curse stretch to its absolute limit, regardless of population size. 14th Generation vampires will never be able to breed true consistently, and thus the population of Caitiff and Thin Bloods swells. Time of thin blood ensues, Antediluvians wake due to murder of all the Caitiff, the end.<br /> <br /> My alternate theory is that Generation works precisely as written, but Gehenna comes in cycles. Every time the Kindred population gets too big, the Antediluvians wake up, devour most of their childer, and Embrace a few Methusalehs so there'll be something to feast on when they wake up again. The Jyhad is merely a way of fostering conflict so that more childer will be Embraced. The modern nights are reaching the end of the most recent cycle. Yes, it will mean the death of most Kindred, but life on earth will go on, and there will be new vampires to populate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to make no difference between thinbloods or clanless. Caitiffs are clanless, not thinbloods. They are not the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T05:02:14-08:00","id":335987,"title":"","content":"My head cannon: [Brujah] is Ilyes, and was seemingly destroyed by Troile. Ilyes founded Ilium (of &quot;The Iliad&quot; fame) and sired Troile there. When Troile usurped Ilyes' position, she renamed Ilium as Troy. The Trojan War was an attempt at vengeance by Menele and other 4th gen Brujah Methuselahs in Greece for the supposed slaying of their sire (who actually escaped with Temporis). At the fall of Troy, Troile fled and founded Carthage. The ferocity of the battle on both sides of the Trojan war switched the original Trujah weakness for the new Brujah one and the Brujah were forced to forget Temporis for Celerity to keep up with the fighting, and the remaining Trujah are the descendants of the few Brujah that didn't partake in the Trojan war. Those Brujah that know (or remember) think of the Trujah much like soldiers thought of Conciencious Objectors during WWI.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4503-cheezewizz2000","user":"Cheezewizz2000","date":". 12-10-2014, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4503-cheezewizz2000","name":"Cheezewizz2000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T16:30:48-08:00","id":336423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119509#post119509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason there are no values beyond &quot;3rd generation&quot; is because it's not such a thing - it's the power level of Clan Founders (the wise kindred among the 3rd, 4th and even unlawfully embraced 5th generations that had reached level 10 Roads/Dharmas &amp; disciplines) and the First Cursed (that has a bunch of 10s in disciplines instead of just those that would shape the clans).<br /> Enoch, Irad, Zilla and many other unnamed ones would drop to what we know as 4th, 5th, 6th, 7th, 8th and worse generations according to their individual accomplishments or lack of them up to that point, a badge of secret shame through the following ages, made the lesser of their brethen and childer by failures of their own spirits. So it's possible for one to be both &quot;Antediluvian&quot; and &quot;4th generation&quot; or much, much worse... though admitedly the absolute majority of the lesser ones destroyed themselves long before the modern age.<br /> <br /> Those at the peak of their Roads/Dharmas, the wisest individiual among 3rd, 4th and even unlawfully embraced 5th generations, would become the Clan Founders while many other vampires that were &quot;antediluvian&quot; in origin, those of the 2nd generation among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've enjoyed this whole thread, but I've come back to this several times. I remember in the Lestat novels (which influenced this), and Lestat learns in Armand's cemetary that some neonates are buried to be entombed forever. The general idea was that in their own way they were titans, too powerful to be permitted to exist. You know, the kind of people who are indomitable. Who are sufficiently different to found a clan? Even if they aren't 2nd generation. Or even fourth? The notion that you can function as higher generation, whether that is mechanically buying higher generation or Golconda's promise of allowing discipline levels normally restricted by generation is enticing. Well said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T22:37:06-08:00","id":336780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheezewizz2000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=335987#post335987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My head cannon: [Brujah] is Ilyes, and was seemingly destroyed by Troile. Ilyes founded Ilium (of &quot;The Iliad&quot; fame) and sired Troile there. When Troile usurped Ilyes' position, she renamed Ilium as Troy. The Trojan War was an attempt at vengeance by Menele and other 4th gen Brujah Methuselahs in Greece for the supposed slaying of their sire (who actually escaped with Temporis). At the fall of Troy, Troile fled and founded Carthage. The ferocity of the battle on both sides of the Trojan war switched the original Trujah weakness for the new Brujah one and the Brujah were forced to forget Temporis for Celerity to keep up with the fighting, and the remaining Trujah are the descendants of the few Brujah that didn't partake in the Trojan war. Those Brujah that know (or remember) think of the Trujah much like soldiers thought of Conciencious Objectors during WWI.</div> </div> </div> </div>That IS a cool idea. I might steal it if I need to use the True Brujah more in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T01:27:01-08:00","id":336840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Enoch in the Shadowlands is in fact Chorazin.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very familiar with Chorazin but not so much informed about Enoch in the Shadowlands. Could you explain this one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/629-anda","name":"anda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T14:23:19-08:00","id":337421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>original_anarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=187071#post187071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the Lasombra Antediluvian very fascinating.<br /> It's so obvious no one really knows what It was all about - even Montano confesses to be ignorant of Its history and motives in the Lasombra Trilogy. And yet we know it to be a creature of such great passions and intense desires that overshadow (no pun intended) any rational approach to It.<br /> <br /> It codified strict laws for It's descendants. It was known to be a wanderer, roaming the world. It's progeny never seemed to live up to Its standards. It often ruled directly over It's offspring, serving as a great Patriarch, the final authority of it's line. It was so intimately connected to darkness that all names and titles people gave to It reflected that (for example the King of Shadows).<br /> <br /> So what if the line of Lasombra was supposed to be the kingship Clan, the heirs of Caine. Imagine Lasombra being embraced by someone of the Second generation as a tribute to their Dark Father. Driven by passions, ruling by strength, crafting a kingdom within darkness.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra Clan symbol is a black crown after all, their ancient symbol for their claim to the legacy of Caine. The Ventrue Clan symbol on the other hand is a sceptre, which in this theory reflects the Ventrue originally intended as a Vizier line.<br /> <br /> Then on the other hand, like has been pointed out by MrAshur for instance, a case can also be made for connecting Lasombra to Lilith (Queen of Night, connected to waters, growing through pain, etc).<br /> <br /> I like the Lasombra antediluvian, there are so many directions you can go with It<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I have been thiinking all day about the ideas above. I am thinking of a &quot;friends of the night&quot; within the friends of the night, low-generation Lasombra who ensure the Clan and Sabbat alike continue this tradition of leadership from the shadows. It's about having power without visibly wielding it, of being the invisible hand that manipulates the Clan, Sabbat and Camarilla alike. The kind who cultivate a young protege, creating childer so that promising young &quot;Erebus&quot; can advance in generation and power. They ensure a hidden hierarchy of low-generation childer cultivated solely by merit and usefulness. It's better than any blood bond! A pure meritocracy with the reward being Generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T15:04:11-08:00","id":337437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=181769#post181769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now I have some time, so here is my interpenetration for how all of the Antediluvians are live an well:<br /> *Lasombra ==Used his &quot;death&quot; in order to become into an Abyssal entity. May be on the verge of becoming an Onceborn.<br /> *Malkav == Became the Madness Network. Where his body is is irrelevant, unless it is going to be diablerized by someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see some sample stats of a Onceborn. Anyone got a link in the wiki or have any information on them?<br /> <br /> For that matter, what if Malkav was the Hive Mind in the underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T01:28:45-08:00","id":337881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=118820#post118820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally a fan of the &quot;three by ten&quot; translation of the Book of Nod, suggesting somewhere in the neighborhood of thirty Antediluvians as opposed to thirteen. My own personal take on where they went is that the Thirteen are the ones who got off easy by begging mercy from Caine, and the remaining Unrepentant were punished far more unspeakably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit do I like that. Holy shit can I use that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4407-loving-the-gorgon","name":"Loving the Gorgon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4407_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T01:51:01-08:00","id":337887,"title":"","content":"I've written a scenario for playing (unnamed) third generation Vampires through several important scenes, such as the rebellion against the second generation and the founding of the Second City. In this story, there are several Antediluvians who never broke Caine's rule about not Embracing. I've let some of those survive to modern nights, sometimes pulling strings in the background, and on at least one occasion interacting with PCs. I like running games with a high power level, since many of the most interesting lore stuff is about characters normal PCs never get the chance to encounter. Having more than thirteen Antediluvians is only logical, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T08:35:23-08:00","id":340054,"title":"","content":"Caine existed but he is deader than dead, to put it like that. There is an apocryphical book of Old Testament that mentions that Cain was killed by accident by a blind archer that had no knowledge of his deed and thus there was no guilt to ascribe to him. Caine was killed that way, 'avenged sevenfold' thing thus did not trigger. Was it a mere accident or was there a hand of God there who ran out of patience?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T11:40:28-08:00","id":340157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>original_anarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=187071#post187071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the Lasombra Antediluvian very fascinating.<br /> Directly below is some information about the Antediluvian from various books - see if it reminds you about anybody else:<br /> <br /> It codified strict laws for It's descendants. It was known to be a wanderer, roaming the world. It's progeny never seemed to live up to Its standards. It often ruled directly over It's offspring, serving as a great Patriarch, the final authority of it's line. It was so intimately connected to darkness that all names and titles people gave to It reflected that (for example the King of Shadows).<br /> <br /> It kind of reminds me of what we think we know about Caine.<br /> <br /> So what if the line of Lasombra was supposed to be the kingship Clan, the heirs of Caine. Imagine Lasombra being embraced by someone of the Second generation as a tribute to their Dark Father. Driven by passions, ruling by strength, crafting a kingdom within darkness.<br /> I can also see Caine not liking that picture of himself, Caine being a vain creature that never ever did anything wrong (notice his rationales for killing his own brother). So Caine, instead favoured others of the Third generation, including the Ventrue Antediluvian, and the Second generation were influenced to do the same. In some sense the Jyhad among the Antediluvians may have started here, about the mantle of Caine, shaking the Second City after the murders of the Second generation.<br /> The Lasombra Clan symbol is a black crown after all, their ancient symbol for their claim to the legacy of Caine. The Ventrue Clan symbol on the other hand is a sceptre, which in this theory reflects the Ventrue originally intended as a Vizier line.</div> </div> </div> </div>That made this sort of pop out of my head.<br /> <br /> Dearest Veronica;<br /> <br /> In our last conversation, you had commented on the ring I wear, and yes indeed it seems curious for a Magister to wear an inverted symbol of our Clan. You have been diligent in your studies it would appear, and friends often notice what others do not. Gunnar would be proud, had he survived, and so now it is time to learn and choose.<br /> <br /> The name we use does not matter at this time, as you can learn these details later. What is important now is that you know the truth about your history. The Noddists are fools, scrabbling over scraps of second hand stories from those who never knew the whole truth! You have come to me, and for the first time you are ready to understand your conceptions of power are insufficient.<br /> <br /> You are a slave, Veronica. Although you are a member of the 9<sup>th</sup> generation you have not achieved a fraction of the potential that you are capable of. The Camarilla prattles on about diablerie and do you know why? Because it stops vampiric evolution. You are aware that your Potence or other powers will reach a finite limit, your fine intelligence or other abilities can only advance so far. You are aware that elders can be smarter, stronger and wield powers you cannot command. Too powerful to be a servant, but not powerful enough to be a master.<br /> <br /> And that is why the crown is inverted, Veronica. It lies waiting to be picked up. Few realize the crown is our symbol because we were the lords of the 1<sup>st</sup> city. We imposed laws upon our kindred, ruling openly but also through the shadows if intrigue and influence when rulership was inappropriate. But always the blood, always one must have the power of the blood.<br /> <br /> You recognized my ring because Gunnar taught you well. I have decided to invest in you, dearest one. I have a childe, I shall command him to embrace two kine, and they shall be for you. You will rise to the 7<sup>th</sup> tomorrow, but your education will begin tonight. I know you search for an Ancient, and I will help you. We will find it and bind it, and Embrace childer and rise in generation if fortune favors us both. Others will help that I will introduce you too, teaching secrets and powers that as yet are unguessed to you and their aid shall be rewarded as well.<br /> <br /> You must choose, dearest Childe. Will you accept our aid, joining us as we seek Apotheosis together? Do you have the courage to take the road to becoming an Antediluvian yourself? Or were you unworthy after all, and need disappear into the ash heap of unpitying history?<br /> <br /> I will have your answer now. Turn and answer, as I am here in the shadows.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T19:24:45-08:00","id":340362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=340054#post340054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caine existed but he is deader than dead, to put it like that. There is an apocryphical book of Old Testament that mentions that Cain was killed by accident by a blind archer that had no knowledge of his deed and thus there was no guilt to ascribe to him. Caine was killed that way, 'avenged sevenfold' thing thus did not trigger. Was it a mere accident or was there a hand of God there who ran out of patience?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Is this real world appocrypha? If so do you know the name of the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T20:01:18-08:00","id":340403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=340362#post340362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this real world appocrypha? If so do you know the name of the book?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>The Book of Jasher, 2:26-30</b><br /> 26 And Lamech was old and advanced in years, and his eyes were dim that he could not see, and Tubal Cain, his son, was leading him and it was one day that Lamech went into the field and Tubal Cain his son was with him, and whilst they were walking in the field, Cain the son of Adam advanced towards them; for Lamech was very old and could not see much, and Tubal Cain his son was very young.<br /> 27 And Tubal Cain told his father to draw his bow, and with the arrows he smote Cain, who was yet far off, and he slew him, for he appeared to them to be an animal.<br /> 28 And the arrows entered Cain's body although he was distant from them, and he fell to the ground and died.<br /> 29 And the Lord requited Cain's evil according to his wickedness, which he had done to his brother Abel, according to the word of the Lord which he had spoken.<br /> 30 And it came to pass when Cain had died, that Lamech and Tubal went to see the animal which they had slain, and they saw, and behold Cain their grandfather was fallen dead upon the earth.<br /> 31 And Lamech was very much grieved at having done this, and in clapping his hands together he struck his son and caused his death.<br /> 32 And the wives of Lamech heard what Lamech had done, and they sought to kill him.<br /> 33 And the wives of Lamech hated him from that day, because he slew Cain and Tubal Cain, and the wives of Lamech separated from him, and would not hearken to him in those days.<br /> 34 And Lamech came to his wives, and he pressed them to listen to him about this matter.<br /> 35 And he said to his wives Adah and Zillah, Hear my voice O wives of Lamech, attend to my words, for now you have imagined and said that I slew a man with my wounds, and a child with my stripes for their having done no violence, but surely know that I am old and grey-headed, and that my eyes are heavy through age, and I did this thing unknowingly.<br /> 36 And the wives of Lamech listened to him in this matter, and they returned to him with the advice of their father Adam, but they bore no children to him from that time, knowing that God's anger was increasing in those days against the sons of men, to destroy them with the waters of the flood for their evil doings.<br /> 37 And Mahlallel the son of Cainan lived sixty-five years and he begat Jared; and Jared lived sixty-two years and he begat Enoch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1026-trudge","user":"trudge","date":". 12-14-2014, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1026-trudge","name":"trudge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1026_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T20:07:20-08:00","id":340407,"title":"","content":"<b>The Second Book of Adam and Eve, 13:5-12</b><br /> 5 Meanwhile Cain, ever since God had cast him off, and had cursed him with trembling and terror, could neither settle nor find rest in any one place; but wandered from place to place.<br /> 6 In his wanderings he came to Lamech's wives, and asked them about him. They said to him, &quot;He is in the field with the cattle.&quot;<br /> 7 Then Cain went to look for him; and as he came into the field, the young shepherd heard the noise he made, and the cattle herding together from before him.<br /> 8 Then said he to Lamech, &quot;O my lord, is that a wild beast or a robber?&quot;<br /> 9 And Lamech said to him, &quot;Make me understand which way he looks, when he comes up.&quot;<br /> 10 Then Lamech bent his bow, placed an arrow on it, and fitted a stone in the sling, and when Cain came out from the open country, the shepherd said to Lamech, &quot;Shoot, behold, he is coming.&quot;<br /> 11 Then Lamech shot at Cain with his arrow and hit him in his side. And Lamech struck him with a stone from his sling, that fell upon his face, and knocked out both his eyes; then Cain fell at once and died.<br /> 12 Then Lamech and the young shepherd came up to him, and found him lying on the ground. And the young shepherd said to him, &quot;It is Cain our grandfather, whom thou hast killed, O my lord!&quot;<br /> 13 Then was Lamech sorry for it, and from the bitterness of his regret, he clapped his hands together, and struck with his flat palm the head of the youth, who fell as if dead; but Lamech thought it was a feint; so he took up a stone and smote him, and smashed his head until he died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1026-trudge","name":"trudge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1026_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T07:00:39-08:00","id":343858,"title":"","content":"I prefer the concept of Arikel and Malkov being twins. In a way the Toreador have an air of occasional sociopathery (which is considered a derangement) and fickleness that can make them as psychologically dangerous as any Malkavian. In their urge to feel the aspects of humanity that they lost when becoming Vampires, you could say it's a bit of a madness on it's own. As for Saulot, I see the &quot;brother&quot; title as more of a term of endearment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T09:57:36-08:00","id":343953,"title":"","content":"Also my personal interpretation is that Antediluvians are not overwhelmingly stronger than majority of 4th Gens because of their thicker vampiric blood but because their mortal selves are closer to Adam Kadmon than post-deluge humanity. That factors matters more than Generation.<br /> <br /> Of course it's one of reasons why Lilith is so strong even if she is nominally human because she is Awakened/Mage. She is an equal to Adam Kadmon which seperated into Adam and Eve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T17:51:03-08:00","id":344278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>g3taso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=337437#post337437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would love to see some sample stats of a Onceborn. Anyone got a link in the wiki or have any information on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a minor one statted out in the final book of the Orpheus line. As I recall, it wasn't terribly impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T06:05:06-08:00","id":344604,"title":"","content":"I think there were only seven antediluvians. In the Enoch, the earliest sects were the Cainites and Lilitu. This philosophical division was strong enough, that it caused the clans to split, much like how the Sabbat antitribu feel culturally separated from their parent clan. It happened so early in the clan histories that these antitribu divisions became codified into completely different clans.<br /> <br /> Arrikel's clan would split into the Toreador (Cainite) and Brujah (Lilitu). Ishtar and Arrikel are alternate names for Ilyes and Troile. To the Brujah, one of their own diablerized the founder. To the Toreador, their founder was slain by an outsider, but over time they've become confused as to which one.<br /> <br /> [Lasombra]'s clan would split into the Ventrue (Cainite) and the Lasombra (Lilitu). Mithra's early death by Troile would simply transform him into a creature of shadow.<br /> <br /> Malkav's clan would split into the Tzimisce (Cainite) and the Malkavian (Lilitu). One embraced chaos physically, the other mentally. The elder's mind resides in the madness network, and his body resides under NYC.<br /> <br /> Absimiliard's clan would split into the Assamite (Cainite) and the Nosferatu (Lilitu). One would hunt monsters, and the other became monsters. The Niktuku are actually the remnants of the proto-clan, sharing aspects of both Assamite and Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> Set's children were never swayed by either Caine or Lilith; instead they embraced Set's own teachings (Setite). Eventually, they withdrew from Enoch's politics completely.<br /> <br /> Ennoia's clan would split into the Ravnos (Cainite) and Gangrel (Lilitu). The week of nightmares in 1999 affected the two clans differently: the Ravnos violently self destructed while the Gangrel are slowly withdrawing from the world, forsaking friends and allies, to dwindle and vanish, to eventually go the way of the Salubri and the Cappadocians.<br /> <br /> Ashur's clan would split into the Salubri (Cainite) and Cappadocian (Lilitu). Tremere diablerized Saulot/Ashur, which also caused the downfall of the Cappadocians, and the Baali to recede from a widespread theat in the middle ages to a minor footnote in modern nights. This implies that Cappadocius was gone/impersonated by the time Augustus tried to embrace him. My guess is that [Lasombra], having just fakes his own death in the Anarch revolt, killed and replaced Augustus - this gave him a chance to start a new clan and indulge his curiosities about Necromancy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1026-trudge","name":"trudge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1026_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T16:14:55-08:00","id":346222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>anda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=336840#post336840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm very familiar with Chorazin but not so much informed about Enoch in the Shadowlands. Could you explain this one?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is a reference to the Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand book, about the TalMaheRa/True Black Hand conspiracy/gehenna cult that among other things, had a secret citadel in the Shadowlands (aka realm of dead) that their mystics and leaders claimed was the memorian/spiritual shadow of Enoch, the original First City of noddist legend. It also hid some mysterious beings called the Aralu whom they claimed were some of the sleeping Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> Mr Ashur, me and other people in the forums have brought the possibility that the group was quite mistaken and their fortress was actually the spiritual shadow of <b>Chorazin </b>or the Baali labyrinth in Cnossos and the Aralu not even kindred, but some of the demons/spirits/cthonic powers worshipped by them in eras long past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-16-2020, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T03:44:40-08:00","id":354657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=346222#post346222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr Ashur, me and other people in the forums have brought the possibility that the group was quite mistaken and their fortress was actually the spiritual shadow of <b>Chorazin </b>or the Baali labyrinth in Cnossos and the Aralu not even kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok cheers for explaining that one. Santa Claus just gave me Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand so I'll be looking into that theory just for the fun of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/629-anda","name":"anda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T08:30:56-08:00","id":354741,"title":"","content":"Well im being very creative and speculative and i do not know all sourcematerial but i like bringing different stuff together so that all world of dakrness stuff fits in one rough mythology-<br /> <br /> as example i start that in the begining there was fire (god) and water (gaia) (active - passive etc. duality)<br /> <br /> those 2 created the wild, the weaver and the wyrm.<br /> <br /> god + wild created humans, god + weaver made angels and god + wyrm made demons (meaning the influence of those)<br /> <br /> i say that gaia is lilith (incarnated which gods can do) and that lilith / gaia created changing breeds with the weaver, mages with the wild and vampires with the wyrm (using that kain was taught by lilith)<br /> <br /> and the 3 minor aspects interacted as well, creating fae from wild + wyrm while weaver + wyrm created ghosts...<br /> <br /> this bases on the idea that gaia made the human body while god made the human soul so humans and vampires are like a cross over of both.<br /> <br /> it is very speculative but basing on mages and placing god and gaia among &quot;most powerfull gods&quot; seems like it could work as both seemingly are not ascended and caught up in their stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 12-30-2014, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T21:14:01-08:00","id":355437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrAshur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=119038#post119038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a brief time Caine and Lilith ruled Enoch together. Each had his/her own disciples among the 3rd generation. The monstrous and primordial Antediluvians, like Tzimisce and Lasombra, were disciples of Lilith. The more civilized, like Arikel and Ventrue, were disciples of Caine.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Caine was an arrogant, unrepentant murderer playing blood god in Enoch, I'd expect the monstrous ones to be his favorites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T21:55:20-08:00","id":355466,"title":"","content":"I like the notion of the &quot;primordial&quot; and &quot;second generation&quot; cainites. In the case above, one might consider Tzimisce and Lasombra as primordials. What other of the known Antediluvians do yo feel are &quot;primordial&quot;. I might suggest Malkav and Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T22:26:35-08:00","id":355481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>g3taso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=355466#post355466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the notion of the &quot;primordial&quot; and &quot;second generation&quot; cainites. In the case above, one might consider Tzimisce and Lasombra as primordials. What other of the known Antediluvians do yo feel are &quot;primordial&quot;. I might suggest Malkav and Gangrel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ennoia, Malkav, Tzimisce, and Lasombra are likely the least human.<br /> Absimiliard is also often described as pretty monstrous - totally hideous and completely removed from humanity.<br /> <br /> Set and Saulot are both enlightened past human philosophy. <br /> Haqim seems to be very interested in protecting humanity, while being rather removed from humanity.<br /> I don't know where Ravnos falls in all this, but I'm guessing that he's more human than not.<br /> <br /> Troile, Arikel, and Ventru all seem fairly interested in humanity.<br /> Tremere and Augustus are extremely human, due to their relatively young ages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1026-trudge","name":"trudge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1026_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T08:58:04-08:00","id":356641,"title":"","content":"I don't know. Ennoia, outside of in the physical sense (and that was largely due to the older Gangrel Flaw of Animal Features being permanent), isn't really described often as being monstrous as apolitical, though somewhat motherly.<br /> <br /> Malkav is likely the MMN, so monstrous in the sense he is disembodied, but alien, no one knows.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce is, currently mindless/soulless, and more like a carnivorous plant or disease. If it did have it's sentience back, it would very likely be extremely alien. Same with Lasombra, as it has literally merged with the Abyss, and it's will and sentience have been supplanted.<br /> <br /> Absimilard has been overcome with grief and self pity, unable to take every dang thing in existence hating it all at once exists in seclusion. It might be interesting to see how he might react if someone jut gave him a dang hug?<br /> <br /> Troile and Ventru are assumed truly dead, though the insinuation is that Ventrue was a super megalomaniac, viewing all others as his pieces to use and abuse.<br /> <br /> Neither Tremere or Giovanni where close to human even when they where humans, and both are right bastards, now just right bastards with eternity, power, and resources. Tremere new full well exactly what taking the vampiric elixir would do (turn them into vampires and destroying their Avatars), and tricked a hell of a lot of other Mages into doing it, then went on a mass Diablerie and forced his &quot;Childer&quot; to do the same. Then, after the last one, he was locked away inside his own body fighting against the soul of Saulot, so he can't have a humanity any higher than 1 or 2 tops, assuming he even followed Humanity. Power and the Inner Voice, the Beast, and Evil Revelations are also possible, though they too would not be high just because he didn't have any time at all to build them.<br /> <br /> Giovanni might not have even followed Humanity even when he was mortal, and he too lead his Clan-to-be on a mass slaughter and Diablerie campaign. All of the above basically applies to Giovanni as well, except that he likely did have the time, and probably chose not to give a crap.<br /> <br /> All indications about Ravnos point to him being a terribly inhuman creature, perfectly fine killing anything that got in his way, and that includes his own Clan. It's highly likely that he both had an alien Path (or Paradox, original version) as well as nearly maxed out, (as he was able to bring most of his powers into play during the daylight hours of his 3 day solid last stand). I say that because the clouds and tempest wouldn't have mattered, it was still &quot;day time&quot; outside, and he would have been restricted to dice pools and Discipline levels no higher than his Path Rating, and it's basically assured he utilized both Chimeristry and Fortitude 10. If he didn't, holy shit. . . ! ! !<br /> <br /> Haqim, could really go one of two ways. Gehenna presents him pretty definitely as both the Force of Nature of Murder and Diablerie itself, but also, contradictorily as the true judge of his own Clan's inner loyalty and spirituality, (as it hunted down Fatima, but found her worthy and didn't killer her on the spot like it had all other renegade Assamites). One version places him in a sort of combination role of martyr and defender of humanity against the evils of Cainites, while the other presents him as nearly utterly mindless, killing anything at all that happens to be noticed by it as a wandering bloodfog shadow. In either case, no player is likely to ever encounter him and survive, so it's probably not all that relevant.<br /> <br /> Set is currently truly dead and inactive. Should he be resurrected, who knows. Clan propaganda suggest like some of the others, he is a &quot;defender of humanity&quot; in a way, opposed to other Cainites/supernaturals, but, he also 100% believes himself (and is believed by his Clan) to have truly been a god BEFORE becoming a Cainite, if he even is a Cainite, and was generally accepted to have been opposed by every single other Antediluvian, Sect, etc. . . Very likely that he would view everyone as at war with him, and active enemies, probably including even his loyal Clan. Very much the same deal as Ventrue, the world exists for his pleasure, use, and abuse, period, though even more so than with Ventrue, Set knows for a fact that he should rule as he is an actual god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T16:26:54-08:00","id":357027,"title":"","content":"The notion of the TBH having a citadel in the spiritual shadow of Chorazin (or the Baali labyrinth) is awesome. Of course, we would have to assume that it would be hopelessly corrupted by the spiritual malaise of those who live Outside (evil chuckling fading into distance).<br /> <br /> Even if they don't, it would be awesome to explore the other side of Chrorazin, whether necromantically or by Umbra. Any thoughts on potential spiritual denizens of the shadow of Chorazin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T07:41:43-08:00","id":357460,"title":"","content":"I had always assumed that the city was as the books claimed, the shadow of Enoch. The Aralu weren't three dead antediluvian but the imprisoned ghosts of the second generation. The names on the walls are their closest descendants on whom they plan to seek their revenge. I like the idea that the Black Hand fortress may instead be Chorazin. If so, then what lies in the three sarcophagi within the inner sanctum. Are the names of on the walls those who have pledged themselves to Namataru?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T08:59:14-08:00","id":357502,"title":"","content":"It make an interesting possibility, though clearly at least 3 of the 4 are not what people believe they are. It's possible that one of them is Ventrue. In canon, yes, it was the remains of Enoch, but that doesn't really go anywhere outside of Wraith.<br /> <br /> I remember in one of the D&amp;D settings there is a concept that deities can not truly die. Instead, when they die or are deposed, they go to this hidden astral realm that is simply filled with the sleeping bodies of all the deities that have fallen. Some, are just enormous severed heads, floating in the nothingness, other sit unmoving on thrones, others seem like they have just been cast on the ground and left where the landed. Something like that could be cool, especially along with the Pit idea.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've always kind of leaned towards the spiritual remains of the tombs of the Second Generation, with the added implication that there are only 3 known 2nd Gen, but four tombs. Another might be a memorial to those Antediluvians who had been destroyed and their clan's deposed. Again, this is the spiritual fragment of them, not the real ones that have since passed from the earth. The Salubri, Brujah, Cappadocian, and _________? Not likely, but hey.<br /> <br /> I've also been kind of partial to the idea that these four tombs are actually some sort of lock, along the lines of preventing some Gehenna Sign from coming to pass. When Enoch fell, causes a lot of those in the know to worry, but when it later appeared in the underworld, the spiritual remains of the lock where enough to maintain its protection again &lt;whatever&gt;. But, later when Underworld Enoch was obliterated (Oblivionated), that last defense went away instantly, and one of the final events leading to Gehenna happened, (whatever you want it to be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T20:07:33-08:00","id":357982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=357460#post357460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had always assumed that the city was as the books claimed, the shadow of Enoch. The Aralu weren't three dead antediluvian but the imprisoned ghosts of the second generation. The names on the walls are their closest descendants on whom they plan to seek their revenge. I like the idea that the Black Hand fortress may instead be Chorazin. If so, then what lies in the three sarcophagi within the inner sanctum. Are the names of on the walls those who have pledged themselves to Namataru?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Baali have a long a glorious tradition of enticing members of other clans and making them Apostates. It is also said that the first ranks of the Baali were converts (and low generation converts at that). The Aralu could be sleeping Apostates, 4th gen converts from other clans. Perhaps with Obtenebration, since the area was guarded by shadow in the text.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T21:52:41-08:00","id":358037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=118794#post118794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not bad. Here are some of my theories.<br /> <br /> A. Malkav was murdered by his childer. There was no unknown assassin. None of then understood the true power of Malkav. E<br /> <br /> B. Verdatha, Antediluvian of the Ventrue is Saulot. Both have a form of Prey Exclusion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They say the Malkavians carry the essence of Malkav within them. Little did anyone know how right they were. The entire clan from the oldest elder to the youngest neonate is, in fact, Malkav himself. The Antediluvian's consciousness was split between multiple bodies existing in several locations simultaneously! Each new childer embraced into the clan provides an additional body for Malkav to inhabit and control. The power of omnipresence is quite a strain on the ancient madman, causing his speech and actions to become incomprehensible to those limited to a single body!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T07:03:44-08:00","id":358289,"title":"","content":"I have a few theories. Probably wont get them all in this post, and I wont go into a lot of detail.<br /> <br /> One is that Ravana and Ennoia are in fact the same being, a 2nd Generation Cainite that was more akin to some primordial, demonic beast than anything even remotely human. An Indian Rakshasa, one might say. It split into two by that high level Protean power, or a stronger variation of it, and became two Antedilluvians.<br /> <br /> Another is that Saulot is Ventrue. He was embraced as the Vizier of the First City, and Lasombra as it's King in Caine's stead, but Caine resented Lasombra because it reflected the Father's great sin of pride, and instead he chose Ventrue as King, and his Clan were groomed into leaders. The two Clans have obviously been at odds about it ever since. Ventrue himself, however, didn't like this outcome at all, and utilized it's immense power of Dominate to fake it's own death and drift from the memories of it's contemporaries, and left for the East, where he became Saulot, and upon his return the Salubri were born, now possesed of a mystical third Eye but a weakness eerily reminiscent of the Ventrue. The reason his death didn't affect the Ventrue is because when he left for the East, he severed his conection with his old Clan mystically, through some power now lost to history. He was the kind of person who is never satisfied, and in one of his more fickle moments he created the Baali, which he soon realized was a mistake. Later he grew tired and resentful of the Salubri also, and attempted to make yet another Clan, this time by becoming Tremere. It didn't exactly work, yet.<br /> <br /> Also on the subject of one Antedilluvian holding two Clans is the Toreador and Brujah. There is no Arikel, or it's just a second name for Troile, a childe of Ilyes'. The fact that Ilyes was extremely old and powerful, as well as a sorcerer who dabbled in time (True Brujah are an experimental bloodline of his), the fact that by his death his progeny was widespread and hardly in contact any more and the face that Troile ended up eating most of him muddled the bloodlines and over time, produced the Toreador and Brujah.<br /> <br /> Set is a 4th Generation Gangrel with the aspect of the snake and also a sorcerer who ate a member of the Second Generation and became something different than other Methuselahs who devoured Antedilluvians, akin to a strange god that then made the Setites. It's either not powerful enough to contain the power it has, exists in another plane, or has been defeated and scattered, or any combination of the three.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4234-bodhiofur","name":"BodhiofUr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T12:07:38-08:00","id":358465,"title":"","content":"Of note to support BodhiofUr the Dark Ages Salubri clanbook specifically mentions Saulot was embraced during the age of the second city not the first. A charade created by Ventru to establish his new identity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T13:00:54-07:00","id":459285,"title":"","content":"There are some really interesting specualtions here. I especially like the Lilith-Lasombra connection.<br /> <br /> Here are a few more: The Aralu were the Messengers of Hunter. They were trapped, but still able to manipulate the Tal'Mahe*Ra to oppose both the Camarilla and the Sabbat. This limited the power of kindred among humans. When Shadow-Enoch fell, they were released, and began to empower Hunters almost immediatly.<br /> <br /> Lasombra, Gangrel, Ravnos, and Tzimisce were embraced by the Crone far outside Enoch. They all have an outsider demenor compared to the middle eastern urban feel of the other clans. And they have unique disciplines that may indicate that they first got a handle on the undead condition apart from other kindred. After all, Gangrel was already described as a shapechanger before going to the city of immortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T15:12:46-07:00","id":461583,"title":"","content":"In my chronicle the Book of Nod is a con job, 90% misinformation and manipulation, 10% truth. It was created after Malkav spoke his prophecy and after the Nosferatu realized very few Kindred were writing down what had actually happened either out of shame or fear. The true prophecy has nothing to do with the destruction of all vampires, it only talks about the total annihilation of the Nosferatu by their founder and his enforcers. This has been manipulated over time to create a sort of security blanket in cainite society for the Nosferatu to hide under. The only reason it talks about Caine at all is that the Book was changed to reflect the Abrahamic religious view of events.<br /> <br /> One version of the vampiric creation tale favored before this was related to Enki and the creation of life and Disease (vampirism). This tends to support the Gilgamesh telling of the Flood myth and the Second City is much more minor.<br /> <br /> The next version is held true by the Setites and has Set as the first vampire cursed by his father Ra for slaying Osiris his brother. For his crime he was cursed not only to never show his face to the sun again but to take the essence of the Chaos serpent Apep unto himself. His wife/Sister Nephthys is a second generation vampire who Sired Anubis also known as Typhon who is the Father of the Setites. Set is tainted by the Chaos Serpent and this gives rise to the discord in Cainite society, the Setites believe that they must corrupt the earth to the point that the Serpent can be drawn forth from Set so that Set may battle and devour it restoring himself in the eyes of Ra. (I hold this one as the accurate myth in so far as any of them are &quot;True&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> Caine/Set == Never died, slumbers under the WEEM-2 oil fields<br /> <br /> *Assamite/Haqim == asleep under the Mountain.<br /> *Brujah == Dead. Soul consumed.<br /> *Cappadocious/Ashur == body diablerized, but soul escaped. Currently rotting Augustus Giovanni's Soul away in order to consume him.<br /> *Gangrel == Alive and well, and sleeping in the Earth, Under the bad lands in New Mexico, shifts position thru the earth every 15 years or so.<br /> *Augustus Giovanni == Slowly going mad as Ashur rots away his soul and consumes him.<br /> *Lasombra/Mekhet == Different folks in my Game, Lasombra body slain, soul escaped into the Abyss. Ability/Desire to return unknown. Mekhet fled into Africa and is in torpor under Ethiopia.<br /> *Malkav == Body destroyed by sunlight after he translated his essence into the Malkavian Madness Network. Not believed to be a concious being.<br /> *Nosferatu/Absimiliard == Slumbers fitfully and moves every 5 years or so, mind is driving the Nictuku to finish their job.<br /> *Ravnos == Ravanna Toast but questions remain as an Indian line was reportedly unaffected.<br /> *Saulot == diablerized but took over Tremere, location unknown.<br /> Anubis/Typhon == slumbers in the valley of Kings. Nephthys sleeps under the Sphinx.<br /> *Toreador/Arikel == alive well, and driving Greece mad with passion.<br /> *Tremere == Goriatrix body, demoted in generation.<br /> *Tzimisce == Believed diablerized; Transubstantiated himself into another reality, the husk left behind was Diablerized and contained only that which Tzimisce had already cast off. Thus the spiritual rot of vissictitude.<br /> *Ventrue/Veddhartha == escaped the Attack though his child Lucien perished, fled to India then the Himalyas, Currently asleep in Nepal.<br /> <br /> The Second Generation:<br /> Nephthys sleeps beneath the Sphinx, wasn't in the Second City to be devoured. None of the Known third Generation Succeeding in claiming the power of the second generation. Set/Caine destroyed the only 2 that succeeded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5237,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5237-frodric","user":"Frodric","date":".  Forgot fate of the Second Generation 03-29-2015, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5237-frodric","name":"Frodric","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T15:58:50-07:00","id":1381124,"title":"","content":"The original kindred of India were the City Gangrel. The bloodline is in fact older than the Gangrel we know. The Indian Gangrel were nearly wiped out by the Ravnos, and had to leave India, starting a feud between the clans.<br /> <br /> (The vampire myth we know is in fact Indian in origin and came to Eastern Europe by the silk road. It refers to creatures with glowing red eyes, claws and which turn into bats.)<br /> <br /> The Ventrue, which admit to having no Antediluvian and who are suspiciously absent from early Kindred history between the mythic age of the second city and the rise of Rome, are in fact a bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T21:47:47-07:00","id":1381208,"title":"","content":"A short number of mine:<br /> <br /> * The Crone is Lilith. This is one that's very popular and almost certainly true. Lilith is a 2nd generation vampire with Thaumaturgy who assumed a dark visage (or simply aged even with her old blood) before tricking Caine into loving her. She is a harbinger of Gehenna and the mother of her own Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> * There's a huge number of non-13 Clans spread throughout the world. There's local ones to South America, China, and other places with perhaps as many as fifty. It should be noted that while Caine is the originator of the vampire myth, he's a figure from Africa originally so this expansion is something that just reflects modern world elements.<br /> <br /> * Malkav and Saulot are the same Antediluvian. They're the Before and After Golconda. No one knows which.<br /> <br /> * They might also be brothers.<br /> <br /> * Saulot embraced the Baali as a revenge Embrace. It was meant as a punishment and resulted in a bunch of 4th generation Infernalists running around. Saulot spent the next few millennia hunting them.<br /> <br /> * Caine created the Six Traditions. He expressly forbid Diablerie, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T14:42:34-07:00","id":1381766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories#post118767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Augustus Giovanni believes the True Vessel contains the remaining blood of Cappadocious and the people who participared in the ritual generally believe it to contain the mortal blood of Augustus, only the traitor knew that it contains the remnant of the blood used to embrace Augustus -that of the Lasombra Antediluvian</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I just say that I love the little bit of validation that V5 has given this, now that Necromancy and Obtenebration have been revealed/retconned as one and the same discipline?<br /> <br /> Beckett is famous for his Noddist theory that Cain's murder of his brother Abel was a literary allegory for a conflict between hunter and gatherer tribes. He should have been looking much further back. The Earth is much older than early Jewish and Christian patriarchs knew, and the legend of Cain and Abel represents a genocidal war between species of pre- human hominds.<br /> <br /> So does the Garou legend of the Impergium.<br /> <br /> The alien and unintelligble motivations of some of the Antedeluvians can be ascribed to the fact that they have pre-human brains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 04-15-2020, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T14:57:24-07:00","id":1381768,"title":"","content":"The Crone is the mother of the Lhiannan bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T16:06:13-07:00","id":1381791,"title":"","content":"I like to think, for the Tal'Mahe'Ra, they think they found Enoch. Except its not. Its actually this place: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/K%C3%A2sdej%C3%A2\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/K%C3%A2sdej%C3%A2</a><br /> <br /> and the Aralu are just slumbering Angels and/or Fallen that become the Heralds of the Imbued when it gets nuked in revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T06:57:37-07:00","id":1381907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=1381791#post1381791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to think, for the Tal'Mahe'Ra, they think they found Enoch. Except its not. Its actually this place: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/K%C3%A2sdej%C3%A2\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/K%C3%A2sdej%C3%A2</a><br /> <br /> and the Aralu are just slumbering Angels and/or Fallen that become the Heralds of the Imbued when it gets nuked in revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! I did that too! Great Minds and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T15:52:51-07:00","id":1383238,"title":"","content":"Here is an off-the-wall one:<br /> <br /> Older editions give lie to Osiris claim that he never sired, but it has been said that his childer all died in his final clash with Set. Now Osiris lamented to Isis his wife that since he entered into the cursed unlife, he had gained the strength of ten bulls (potence), his words could sway the hearts of men (presence) and he could make even the rive Nile run backwards (Temporis?), but his own passions were cold and dead. Back in the day this was taken to mean that Osiris sire Typhon was Brujah. However, I do no think Osiris generation has even been stated outright.<br /> <br /> If Typhon was of the Second Generation, it could be Osiris that founded the Trujah and those who say the Trujahs claim to being the true descendants of Brujah are a lie could be right. Any get of Osiris that crawled away from that lost battle would need to keep firmly shut about his real lineage or Set would finish the job.<br /> <br /> Supporting information is the fact that the Trujah are said to have been postponing their vengeance for 5000 years, putting them at precisely the right time, and that the sarcophagus of Irad were found in the general area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T02:23:59-07:00","id":1383315,"title":"","content":"One would be: It's just a Myth.<br /> Noddism, The book of Nod etc. is just a religious/mythological explanation Vampires came up with over time, it has nothing/little to do with actual Truth. The first Generation might even consist of more then one being. Maybe they came to be together at the same point in time, maybe they arose individually.<br /> <br /> <br /> The other: Settites are the closest to the Truth<br /> Set was the first \u201cVampire\u201d or at least the progenitor of Vampires, he killed his brother Osiris. Horus(who is maybe Helios) cursed Kindred with the weakness of fire and sunlight. The thirst for blood is not really a curse leveled upon them by anyone, blood is simply what fuels their existence and power. The Beast is an aspect of Set the Destroyer passed down through every Vampire.<br /> This Truth was muddied over time and later reformulated by Christian and later also Islamic Kindred through their cultural lens informed by the Cain and Abel story.<br /> <br /> Who/What was/is Set? A mortal/awakened? A Spirit/Godling? An aspect of the Wyrm? A dead person who fund a way back to life?(This was way before the underworld, and presumably ghosts, even remotely resembled what it is today) Maybe he himself isn't even a real Vampire, only their creator.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T03:51:35-07:00","id":1383323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories#post118767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> While Augustus Giovanni believes the True Vessel contains the remaining blood of Cappadocious and the people who participared in the ritual generally believe it to contain the mortal blood of Augustus, only the traitor knew that it contains the remnant of the blood used to embrace Augustus -that of the Lasombra Antediluvian.</div> </div> </div> </div> I really like that idea. Especially under V5 where Necromancy and Obtenebration have the same root discipline(Oblivion). And it is(to me at least) also heavily implied in 5V that the Abyss that Lasombra traditionally view as the source of their Obtenebration, is in fact Oblivion(as in the that which lies beneath the Labyrinth in Wraith).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T09:33:15-07:00","id":1383783,"title":"","content":"The Clans of Kindred are divided into two camps: the Clans of Caine and the Clans of Lilith. The first Gehenna (as alluded to in Beckett's Jyhad Diary) was a civil war between the members of the Second and Third Generations who either sided with Caine or Lilith depending on how they felt about Lilith's story that Caine betrayed her. The Laibon are descended from Methuselahs or Antediluvians who decided to stay neutral and basically just stopped talking about Caine, hence the reason why the Laibon are so very close to Cainites in some regards, but very different in others.<br /> <br /> Eventually, the tide of the first Gehenna War turned against Lilith, and she and whatever loyal Kindred she had left fled across the Atlantic to the Americas. Lilith and her Clans started to make their Havens in bodies of water deep enough to shield them from the sun as a way of ritually distinguishing themselves from the traitor Caine and his pawns. Hence the reason why the Ancestor in <i>CbN V5 </i>and its &quot;Cultivar&quot; cult are intrigued by the Bahari: they are Cainites who have rejected Caine's propaganda and support Lilith. This also means that the Drowned who have been referenced in BJD and V5 are the Clans of Lilith. By extension, this implies that the Pisanob are Drowned who infiltrated the Giovanni/Hecata, and the Tlacique are descended from a blood sibling of Set, my money being on Anhur, Bastet, or Sekhmet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T09:40:21-07:00","id":1383784,"title":"","content":"A unified theory that incorporates the concept of cyclical Gehenna to allow for all of these weirdly divergent clans, as well as the &quot;old Earth&quot; idea that I keep flogging:<br /> <br /> The clan founders that we know of, the 13 acknowledged by the predominant clans, are just the survivors of previous Gehennas who diablerized the ones who came before. This is mythologized by the Bahari in the form of the Cainite assault on Lilith's garden.<br /> <br /> A lot of these exotic phenotypes out on the periphery are the children of the devoured and the forgotten, as abandoned by fate as the Salubri.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 04-25-2020, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T14:03:06-07:00","id":1383840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/118767-your-noddist-fan-theories?p=1383784#post1383784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A unified theory that incorporates the concept of cyclical Gehenna to allow for all of these weirdly divergent clans, as well as the &quot;old Earth&quot; idea that I keep flogging:<br /> <br /> The clan founders that we know of, the 13 acknowledged by the predominant clans, are just the survivors of previous Gehennas who diablerized the ones who came before. This is mythologized by the Bahari in the form of the Cainite assault on Lilith's garden.<br /> <br /> A lot of these exotic phenotypes out on the periphery are the children of the devoured and the forgotten, as abandoned by fate as the Salubri.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Nightshade&quot; scenario from <i>Gehenna </i>involves a scene where the player coterie goes to the ruins of the Second City and find statues of 23 Antediluvians. Considering the fact that V5 seems to be borrowing some plot ideas from various Gehenna scenarios, I wouldn't be surprised if it comes to light that, yeah, there were more Antediluvians than just 13, and that some of the weirder bloodlines without clear-cut origins trace back to these &quot;lost&quot; Antediluvians and lost their &quot;clan&quot; status over the long millennia. Hell, we've seen it happen with the Salubri and Ravnos, wouldn't be a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T16:59:37-07:00","id":1383868,"title":"","content":"First off I just wanna say that those books of apocrypha sound really interesting and I need to check them out someday.<br /> <br /> Anyway now, to share some Noddist head canons of my own:<br /> <br /> \u2022There were seven, or at least seven, members of the second generation embraced by Caine. They were the King and Queen of Enoch, Enoch, Irad, Zillah, The Crone, and Dracion. The city of Enoch had the misfortune of being one of the earliest settlements while also not knowing the tale of Caine's exile. They welcomed him into the city and he slowly grew to take power over it through control of and the eventual embrace of the King and Queen. However Enoch's discovery led to the young prince's embrace and a series of tragedies that saw the king and queen destroy themselves, beginning the dark path of Caine's brood.<br /> <br /> \u2022Enoch (the wise, to lead) and Irad (the strong, to battle) were kindred of The First City and so was Zillah (the beautiful, to comfort) who Caine had embraced for compassion. Caine's curse was to wander though and his desire to be loved compelled him to find a wise woman who promised to help him. This was The Crone...<br /> <br /> \u2022The Crone was not Lilith herself, but a follower of Lilith, one of the first bahari and a cultist who sought out Caine to humiliate, pain, and teach him. She later went on to pass the embrace onto Ennoia, Lilith's daughter.<br /> <br /> \u2022Early in Caine's wandering he was alone, weak, and deeply pained. He was found one night by a nomadic people and their leader, a passionate man, lent Caine aid and comfort. In gratitude, Caine offered the man his thanks and loyalty and would eventually show it by embracing him, Dracian, father and eventual sire of Zapasathura.<br /> <br /> \u2022The vampire who eventually wandered down the Nile and discovered the pre-historic Egyptians and spoke to their leader was Dracian. He would watch the domain and eventually decide to embrace both Sutekh the ambitious warrior and Osiris the wise leader. <br /> <br /> \u2022The First City was for a great deal of time the domain of Caine, the three childer who stayed by his side, and their own childer. However in time outsiders such as Ennoia, Sutekh, and Zapasathura would visit Enoch and realizing that his brood may grow beyond his control without careful husbandry, he forbid the third generation to embrace. This was perhaps the beginning of the end as every antediluvian would eventually disobey...<br /> <br /> \u2022The thirteen antediluvians are the most well known of the third generation however there were others in the first city, those who like Caitiff were without the Curses From Caine. Little of these kindred is known, but their legacy remains...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}